DG.put("krisnaavtaar/80",{"n":80,"title":"ਅਥ ਊਖਾ ਕੋ ਬਿਆਹ ਕਥਨੰ। ਦਸ ਸੈ ਭੁਜਾ ਕੋ ਗਰਬੁ ਹਰਨ ਕਥਨੰ","title_roman":"Ath ookhaa ko biaah kathnan | das sai bhujaa ko garbu haran kathnan","page":675,"blocks":[{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਚੌਪਈ","gurmukhi":"ਚੌਪਈ","roman":"Chaupaee","meaning_en":"Chaupai.","page":675,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[2184],"number_text":"੨੧੮੪।","page":675,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜਦੁਪਤਿ ਪੌਤ੍ਰ ਬ੍ਯਾਹ ਘਰ ਆਯੋ। ਅਤਿ ਚਿਤਿ ਅਪਨੇ ਹਰਖ ਬਢਾਯੋ।","roman":"Jadupti pautr byaah ghar aayo | ati chiti apne harakh badhaayo |","meaning_en":"When the grandson of the Lord of the Yadavs came home married, joy grew greatly in his heart.","page":675,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਜਦੁਪਤਿ ਪੌਤ੍ਰ: Krishna's grandson (Pradyumna's son, Anirudh in what follows); read so."},{"gurmukhi":"ਗਰਬ ਉਤੈ ਦਸ ਸੈ ਭੁਜ ਕੀਨੋ। ਮੈ ਬਰੁ ਮਹਾਰੁਦ੍ਰ ਤੇ ਲੀਨੋ। ੨੧੮੪।","roman":"Garab utai das sai bhuj keeno | mai baru mahaarudr te leeno | 2184 |","meaning_en":"Over there, the thousand-armed one grew proud: \"I have taken a boon from Maharudra.\"","page":675,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਦਸ ਸੈ ਭੁਜ: lit. 'ten hundred arms', i.e. the thousand-armed Banasur."}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","gurmukhi":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","roman":"Savaiyaa","meaning_en":"Savaiya.","page":675,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[2185],"number_text":"੨੧੮੫।","page":675,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਗਾਲ ਬਜਾਇ ਭਲੀ ਬਿਧਿ ਸੋ ਅਰੁ ਤਾਲ ਸਭੋ ਸੰਗਿ ਹਾਥਨ ਦੀਨੋ।","roman":"Gaal bajaai bhalee bidhi so aru taal sabho sangi haathan deeno |","meaning_en":"Sounding his cheeks well and clapping time with his hands,","page":675,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਗਾਲ ਬਜਾਇ: the cheek-sound made in worship of Shiva; read so."},{"gurmukhi":"ਜੈਸੇ ਲਿਖੀ ਬਿਧਿ ਬੇਦ ਬਿਖੈ ਤਿਹ ਭੂਪ ਤਿਹੀ ਬਿਧਿ ਸੋ ਤਪੁ ਕੀਨੋ।","roman":"Jaise likhee bidhi bed bikhai tih bhoop tihee bidhi so tapu keeno |","meaning_en":"just as the method is written in the Vedas, by that same method the king performed austerities.","page":675,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਗਿ ਕਰੇ ਸਭ ਹੀ ਬਿਧਿ ਪੂਰਬ ਕਉਨ ਬਿਧਾਨ ਬਿਨਾ ਨਹੀ ਹੀਨੋ।","roman":"Jagi kare sabh hee bidhi poorab kaun bidhaan binaa nahee heeno |","meaning_en":"He performed sacrifices in every manner prescribed of old, leaving none lacking in any rite.","page":675,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਰੁਦ੍ਰ ਰਿਝਾਇ ਕਹਿਯੋ ਇਹ ਭਾਤਿ ਸੁ ਹੋ ਕੁਟਵਾਰ ਇਹੀ ਬਰੁ ਲੀਨੋ। ੨੧੮੫।","roman":"Rudr rijhaai kahiyo ih bhaati su ho kutvaar ihee baru leeno | 2185 |","meaning_en":"Pleasing Rudra, he spoke thus: \"Be my guardian of the gate\"; this was the boon he took.","page":675,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਕੁਟਵਾਰ: 'kotwal', city guard/warden."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[2186],"number_text":"੨੧੮੬।","page":675,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਰੁਦ੍ਰ ਜਬੈ ਕੁਟਵਾਰ ਕਯੋ ਤਬ ਦੇਸਨਿ ਦੇਸਨ ਧਰਮ ਚਲਾਯੋ।","roman":"Rudr jabai kutvaar kayo tab desni desan dharam chalaayo |","meaning_en":"When Rudra became his guardian, he spread righteousness through land after land.","page":675,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਪਾਪ ਕੀ ਬਾਤ ਗਈ ਛਪ ਕੈ ਸਭ ਹੀ ਜਗ ਮੈ ਜਸੁ ਭੂਪਤਿ ਛਾਯੋ।","roman":"Paap kee baat gaee chhap kai sabh hee jag mai jasu bhoopti chhaayo |","meaning_en":"All talk of sin went into hiding, and the king's fame spread through the whole world.","page":675,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸਤ੍ਰ ਤ੍ਰਿਸੂਲ ਕੈ ਬਸਿ ਭਏ ਅਰਿ ਅਉਰ ਕਿਹੂੰ ਨਹਿ ਸੀਸ ਉਠਾਯੋ।","roman":"Satr trisool kai basi bhae ari aur kihoon nahi sees uthaayo |","meaning_en":"By the trident's power his foes came under his control, and no other enemy raised his head.","page":675,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਸਤ੍ਰ ਤ੍ਰਿਸੂਲ ਕੈ: 'by the trident (of Shiva)'; read so."},{"gurmukhi":"ਲੋਗਨ ਤਉਨ ਸਮੈ ਜਗ ਮੈ ਕਬਿ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਭਨੈ ਅਤਿ ਹੀ ਸੁਖ ਪਾਯੋ। ੨੧੮੬।","roman":"Logan taun samai jag mai kabi syaam bhanai ati hee sukh paayo | 2186 |","meaning_en":"says the poet Shyam: at that time the people in the world found great happiness.","page":675,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[2187],"number_text":"੨੧੮੭।","page":675,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਰੁਦ੍ਰ ਪ੍ਰਤਾਪ ਭਏ ਅਰਿ ਬਸਿ ਕਿਹੂੰ ਅਰਿ ਆਨ ਨ ਸੀਸ ਉਠਾਯੋ।","roman":"Rudr prataap bhae ari basi kihoon ari aan na sees uthaayo |","meaning_en":"By Rudra's glory his enemies were subdued, and no other foe raised his head.","page":675,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਰਿ ਲੈ ਕਬਿ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਭਨੈ ਅਤਿ ਹੀ ਇਹ ਪਾਇਨ ਊਪਰ ਸੀਸ ਝੁਕਾਯੋ।","roman":"Kari lai kabi syaam bhanai ati hee ih paain oopar sees jhukaayo |","meaning_en":"says the poet Shyam, they joined their hands and bowed their heads at his feet.","page":675,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਭੂਪ ਨ ਰੰਚਕ ਬਾਤ ਲਈ ਇਹ ਪਉਰਖ ਮੇਰੋ ਈ ਹੈ ਲਖਿ ਪਾਯੋ।","roman":"Bhoop na ranchak baat laee ih paurakh mero ee hai lakhi paayo |","meaning_en":"The king did not take this to heart at all; he concluded, \"This is my own manliness.\"","page":675,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਪਉਰਖ ਭਯੋ ਭੁਜਦੰਡਨ ਰੁਦ੍ਰ ਤੇ ਜੁਧ ਹੀ ਕੋ ਬਰੁ ਮਾਗਨ ਧਾਯੋ। ੨੧੮੭।","roman":"Paurakh bhayo bhujdandan rudr te judh hee ko baru maagan dhaayo | 2187 |","meaning_en":"Valour swelled in his mighty arms, and he ran to Rudra to ask a boon of battle itself.","page":675,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਸੋਰਠਾ","gurmukhi":"ਸੋਰਠਾ","roman":"Sorthaa","meaning_en":"Sortha.","page":675,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[2188],"number_text":"੨੧੮੮।","page":675,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਮੂਰਖ ਲਹਿਯੋ ਨ ਭੇਦੁ ਜੁਧੁ ਚਹਨਿ ਸਿਵ ਪੈ ਚਲਿਯੋ।","roman":"Moorakh lahiyo na bhedu judhu chahni siv pai chaliyo |","meaning_en":"The fool did not grasp the secret; wishing for war he went to Shiva,","page":675,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਰਿ ਬਿਰਥਾ ਸਭ ਖੇਦਿ ਜਿਵ ਰਵਿ ਤਪ ਬਾਰੂ ਤਪੈ। ੨੧੮੮।","roman":"Kari birthaa sabh khedi jiv ravi tap baaroo tapai | 2188 |","meaning_en":"making all his effort vain, as the sun's heat merely heats the sand.","page":675,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਜਿਵ ਰਵਿ ਤਪ ਬਾਰੂ ਤਪੈ: simile of wasted effort; uncertain."}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"speaker","name":"ਨ੍ਰਿਪ ਬਾਚ ਰੁਦ੍ਰ ਸੋ","gurmukhi":"ਨ੍ਰਿਪ ਬਾਚ ਰੁਦ੍ਰ ਸੋ","roman":"Nrip baach rudr so","meaning_en":"The king said to Rudra:","page":676,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","gurmukhi":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","roman":"Savaiyaa","meaning_en":"Savaiya.","page":676,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[2189],"number_text":"੨੧੮੯।","page":676,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸੀਸ ਨਿਵਾਇ ਕੈ ਪ੍ਰੇਮ ਬਢਾਇ ਕੈ ਯੌ ਨ੍ਰਿਪ ਰੁਦ੍ਰ ਸੋ ਬੈਨ ਸੁਨਾਵੈ।","roman":"Sees nivaai kai prem badhaai kai yau nrip rudr so bain sunaavai |","meaning_en":"Bowing his head and with growing love, the king spoke these words to Rudra:","page":676,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਾਤ ਹੋ ਹਉ ਜਿਹ ਸਤ੍ਰ ਪੈ ਰੁਦ੍ਰ ਜੂ ਕੋਊ ਨ ਆਗੇ ਤੇ ਹਾਥ ਉਠਾਵੈ।","roman":"Jaat ho hau jih satr pai rudr joo ko'oo na aage te haath uthaavai |","meaning_en":"\"O Rudra, whatever enemy I go against, no one raises a hand against me.","page":676,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਾ ਤੇ ਅਯੋਧਨ ਕਉ ਹਮਰੋ ਕਬਿ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਕਹੈ ਮਨੂਆ ਲਲਚਾਵੈ।","roman":"Taa te ayodhan kau hamro kabi syaam kahai manooaa lalchaavai |","meaning_en":"Therefore, says the poet Shyam, my heart longs for battle.","page":676,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਚਾਹਤ ਹੋ ਤੁਮ ਤੇ ਬਰੁ ਆਜ ਕੋਊ ਹਮਰੇ ਸੰਗ ਜੂਝ ਮਚਾਵੈ। ੨੧੮੯।","roman":"Chaahat ho tum te baru aaj ko'oo hamre sang joojh machaavai | 2189 |","meaning_en":"Today I want a boon from you: that someone may wage war with me.\"","page":676,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"speaker","name":"ਰੁਦ੍ਰ ਬਾਚ ਨ੍ਰਿਪ ਸੋ","gurmukhi":"ਰੁਦ੍ਰ ਬਾਚ ਨ੍ਰਿਪ ਸੋ","roman":"Rudr baach nrip so","meaning_en":"Rudra said to the king:","page":676,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਚੌਪਈ","gurmukhi":"ਚੌਪਈ","roman":"Chaupaee","meaning_en":"Chaupai.","page":676,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[2190],"number_text":"੨੧੯੦।","page":676,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਯੌ ਸੁਨਿ ਕੇ ਸਿਵ ਕ੍ਰੋਧ ਬਢਾਯੋ। ਯੌ ਕਹਿ ਕੈ ਤਿਹ ਬਚਨ ਸੁਨਾਯੋ।","roman":"Yau suni ke siv krodh badhaayo | yau kahi kai tih bachan sunaayo |","meaning_en":"Hearing this, Shiva's anger grew, and he spoke these words to him:","page":676,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਬੈ ਧੁਜਾ ਤੁਮਰੀ ਗਿਰ ਪਰਿ ਹੈ। ਤਬੈ ਸੂਰ ਕੋਊ ਤੁਮ ਸੰਗ ਲਰਿ ਹੈ। ੨੧੯੦।","roman":"Jabai dhujaa tumree gir pari hai | tabai soor ko'oo tum sang lari hai | 2190 |","meaning_en":"\"When your banner falls to the ground, then some warrior will fight with you.\"","page":676,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","gurmukhi":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","roman":"Savaiyaa","meaning_en":"Savaiya.","page":676,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[2191],"number_text":"੨੧੯੧।","page":676,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਹ੍ਵੈ ਕਰਿ ਕ੍ਰੋਧ ਜਬੈ ਸਿਵ ਜੂ ਤਿਹ ਭੂਪਤਿ ਕੋ ਤਿਨ ਬੈਨ ਸੁਨਾਯੋ।","roman":"Hvai kari krodh jabai siv joo tih bhoopti ko tin bain sunaayo |","meaning_en":"When Shiva in anger spoke these words to that king,","page":676,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਭੂਪ ਲਖਿਯੋ ਨਹਿ ਭੇਦ ਕਛੂ ਸੁ ਲਖਿਯੋ ਚਿਤ ਚਾਹਤ ਹੋ ਸੋਊ ਪਾਯੋ।","roman":"Bhoop lakhiyo nahi bhed kachhoo su lakhiyo chit chaahat ho so'oo paayo |","meaning_en":"the king did not grasp the secret at all; he thought, \"What my heart wished for, that I have obtained.\"","page":676,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਬਾਗੇ ਕੇ ਭੀਤਰ ਫੂਲਿ ਗਯੋ ਭੁਜ ਦੰਡਨ ਕੋ ਅਤਿ ਓਜ ਜਨਾਯੋ।","roman":"Baage ke bheetar phooli gayo bhuj dandan ko ati oj janaayo |","meaning_en":"He swelled within his robe and showed the great strength of his mighty arms.","page":676,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਬਾਗੇ ਕੇ ਭੀਤਰ ਫੂਲਿ ਗਯੋ: 'swelled inside his jama (robe)', i.e. was overjoyed; idiom."},{"gurmukhi":"ਯੌ ਦਸ ਸੈ ਭੁਜ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਕਹੈ ਅਤਿ ਆਨੰਦ ਸੋ ਫਿਰਿ ਮੰਦਿਰ ਆਯੋ। ੨੧੯੧।","roman":"Yau das sai bhuj syaam kahai ati aanand so phiri mandir aayo | 2191 |","meaning_en":"Thus, says Shyam, the thousand-armed one returned to his palace in great joy.","page":676,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[2192],"number_text":"੨੧੯੨।","page":676,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਏਕ ਹੁਤੀ ਦੁਹਤਾ ਤਿਹ ਕੀ ਤਿਹ ਸੋਤਿ ਨਿਸਾ ਸੁਪਨੋ ਇਕੁ ਪਾਯੋ।","roman":"Ek hutee duhtaa tih kee tih soti nisaa supno iku paayo |","meaning_en":"He had a daughter; while sleeping at night she had a dream.","page":676,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਮੈਨ ਸੋ ਰੂਪ ਅਨੂਪ ਸੀ ਮੂਰਤਿ ਸੋ ਇਹ ਕੇ ਚਲਿ ਮੰਦਿਰ ਆਯੋ।","roman":"Main so roop anoop see moorti so ih ke chali mandir aayo |","meaning_en":"One with a form like Kama, of matchless beauty, came to her chamber.","page":676,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਮੈਨ: Kama, god of love."},{"gurmukhi":"ਭੋਗ ਕੀਯੋ ਤਿਹ ਸੋ ਮਿਲਿ ਕੈ ਇਨਿ ਚਿਤ ਬਿਖੈ ਅਤਿ ਹੀ ਸੁਖ ਪਾਯੋ।","roman":"Bhog keeyo tih so mili kai ini chit bikhai ati hee sukh paayo |","meaning_en":"He joined with her in love-making, and she felt great pleasure in her heart.","page":676,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਚਉਕ ਪਰੀ ਨਹੀ ਪੀਯ ਪਿਖਿਯੋ ਕਬਿ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਕਹੈ ਤਿਨ ਸੋਕ ਜਨਾਯੋ। ੨੧੯੨।","roman":"Chauk paree nahee peey pikhiyo kabi syaam kahai tin sok janaayo | 2192 |","meaning_en":"She started awake and did not see her beloved; says the poet Shyam, she showed great grief.","page":676,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[2193],"number_text":"੨੧੯੩।","page":676,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜਾਗਤਿ ਹੀ ਬਿਰਲਾਪ ਕੀਓ ਅਤਿ ਹੀ ਚਿਤਿ ਸੋਕ ਕੀ ਬਾਤ ਜਨਾਈ।","roman":"Jaagti hee birlaap keeo ati hee chiti sok kee baat janaaee |","meaning_en":"As soon as she woke she wailed and showed the grief in her heart.","page":676,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਅੰਗਨ ਮੈ ਡਗਰੀ ਸੀ ਫਿਰੈ ਪਤਿ ਕੀ ਕਰਿ ਕੈ ਮਨ ਮੈ ਦੁਚਿਤਾਈ।","roman":"Angan mai dagree see phirai pati kee kari kai man mai duchitaaee |","meaning_en":"She wandered the courtyard as if lost, her mind torn over the husband.","page":676,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਡਗਰੀ ਸੀ: 'like one strayed/staggering'; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਪ੍ਰੇਤ ਲਗਿਯੋ ਕਿਧੌ ਪ੍ਰੀਤ ਲਗੀ ਕਿ ਕਛੂ ਅਬ ਯਾ ਠਗਮੂਰੀ ਸੀ ਖਾਈ।","roman":"Pret lagiyo kidhau preet lagee ki kachhoo ab yaa thagmooree see khaaee |","meaning_en":"\"Has a ghost possessed her, or has love taken hold, or has she now eaten some drugging root?\"","page":676,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਠਗਮੂਰੀ: a stupefying herb used by thugs."},{"gurmukhi":"ਭਾਖਤ ਭੀ ਸਖੀ ਮੋ ਕਉ ਅਬੈ ਮੇਰੋ ਦੈ ਗਯੋ ਪ੍ਰੀਤਮ ਆਜ ਦਿਖਾਈ। ੨੧੯੩।","roman":"Bhaakhat bhee sakhee mo kau abai mero dai gayo preetam aaj dikhaaee | 2193 |","meaning_en":"She said, \"Friend, just now my beloved has shown himself to me today.\"","page":676,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[2194],"number_text":"੨੧੯੪।","page":676,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਏਤੀ ਹੀ ਕੈ ਬਤੀਯਾ ਮੁਖ ਤੇ ਗਿਰ ਭੂ ਪੈ ਪਰੀ ਸਭ ਸੁਧਿ ਭੁਲਾਈ।","roman":"Etee hee kai bateeyaa mukh te gir bhoo pai paree sabh sudhi bhulaaee |","meaning_en":"Having spoken only this much from her mouth, she fell to the ground and lost all awareness.","page":676,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਯੌ ਬਿਸੰਭਾਰ ਪਰੀ ਧਰਨੀ ਕਬਿ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਭਨੈ ਮਨੋ ਨਾਗਿਨ ਖਾਈ।","roman":"Yau bisanbhaar paree dharnee kabi syaam bhanai mano naagin khaaee |","meaning_en":"She lay on the earth senseless, says the poet Shyam, as though a she-serpent had bitten her,","page":676,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਮਾਨਹੁ ਅੰਤ ਸਮੋ ਪਹੁਚਿਯੋ ਇਹ ਦੈ ਗਯੋ ਪ੍ਰੀਤਮ ਸੋਤਿ ਦਿਖਾਈ।","roman":"Maanhu ant samo pahuchiyo ih dai gayo preetam soti dikhaaee |","meaning_en":"as if her last moment had come, since her beloved had appeared to her in sleep.","page":676,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਉ ਲਗਿ ਚਿਤ੍ਰ ਰੇਖਾ ਜੁ ਹੁਤੀ ਸੁ ਸਖੀ ਇਹ ਕੀ ਇਹ ਕੇ ਢਿਗਿ ਆਈ। ੨੧੯੪।","roman":"Tau lagi chitr rekhaa ju hutee su sakhee ih kee ih ke dhigi aaee | 2194 |","meaning_en":"Meanwhile Chitrarekha, who was her friend, came to her side.","page":676,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਚੌਪਈ","gurmukhi":"ਚੌਪਈ","roman":"Chaupaee","meaning_en":"Chaupai.","page":677,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[2195],"number_text":"੨੧੯੫।","page":677,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸਖਿਨ ਦਸਾ ਜਬ ਯਾਹਿ ਸੁਨਾਈ। ਚਿਤ੍ਰ ਰੇਖ ਤਬ ਸੋਚ ਜਨਾਈ।","roman":"Sakhin dasaa jab yaahi sunaaee | chitr rekh tab soch janaaee |","meaning_en":"When the friends told her of this state, Chitrarekha then showed concern:","page":677,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਇਹ ਜੀਏ ਜੀਯ ਹੋ ਨਹੀ ਮਰਿ ਹੋ। ਜਾਨਤ ਜਤਨੁ ਏਕ ਸੋਊ ਕਰਿ ਹੋ। ੨੧੯੫।","roman":"Ih jee'e jeey ho nahee mari ho | jaanat jatnu ek so'oo kari ho | 2195 |","meaning_en":"\"If she lives, I live; if not, I will die. I know one remedy, and that I will carry out.","page":677,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"The second half reads lit. 'I will not die'; the sense taken is that the friend's life depends on hers; uncertain."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[2196],"number_text":"੨੧੯੬।","page":677,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜੋ ਮੈ ਨਾਰਦ ਸੋ ਸੁਨਿ ਪਾਯੋ। ਵਹੈ ਜਤਨੁ ਮੇਰੇ ਮਨਿ ਆਯੋ।","roman":"Jo mai naarad so suni paayo | vahai jatnu mere mani aayo |","meaning_en":"What I heard from Narad, that very remedy has come to my mind.","page":677,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਤਨੁ ਆਜ ਸੋਊ ਮੈ ਕਰਿ ਹੋ। ਬਾਨਾਸੁਰ ਤੇ ਨੈਕੁ ਨ ਡਰਿ ਹੋ। ੨੧੯੬।","roman":"Jatnu aaj so'oo mai kari ho | baanaasur te naiku na dari ho | 2196 |","meaning_en":"I will carry out that remedy today and will not fear Banasur in the least.\"","page":677,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"speaker","name":"ਸਖੀ ਬਾਚ ਚਿਤ੍ਰ ਰੇਖਾ ਸੋ","gurmukhi":"ਸਖੀ ਬਾਚ ਚਿਤ੍ਰ ਰੇਖਾ ਸੋ","roman":"Sakhee baach chitr rekhaa so","meaning_en":"The friend said to Chitrarekha:","page":677,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","gurmukhi":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","roman":"Dohraa","meaning_en":"Dohra.","page":677,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[2197],"number_text":"੨੧੯੭।","page":677,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਆਤੁਰ ਹ੍ਵੈ ਤਿਹ ਕੀ ਸਖੀ ਤਿਹ ਕੋ ਕਹਿਯੋ ਸੁਨਾਇ।","roman":"Aatur hvai tih kee sakhee tih ko kahiyo sunaai |","meaning_en":"Distressed, her friend spoke and told her,","page":677,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜੋ ਜਾਨਤ ਹੈ ਜਤਨ ਤੂ ਸੋ ਅਬ ਤੁਰਤੁ ਬਨਾਇ। ੨੧੯੭।","roman":"Jo jaanat hai jatan too so ab turtu banaai | 2197 |","meaning_en":"\"Whatever remedy you know, prepare it quickly now.\"","page":677,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","gurmukhi":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","roman":"Savaiyaa","meaning_en":"Savaiya.","page":677,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[2198],"number_text":"੨੧੯੮।","page":677,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਯੌ ਸੁਨਿ ਕੈ ਤਿਹ ਕੀ ਬਤੀਯਾ ਤਬ ਹੀ ਇਹ ਚਉਦਹ ਲੋਕ ਬਨਾਏ।","roman":"Yau suni kai tih kee bateeyaa tab hee ih chaudah lok banaae |","meaning_en":"Hearing her words, she at once drew the fourteen worlds,","page":677,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜੀਵ ਜਨਾਵਰ ਦੇਵ ਨਿਸਾਚਰ ਭੀਤ ਕੇ ਬੀਚ ਲਿਖੇ ਚਿਤ ਲਾਏ।","roman":"Jeev janaavar dev nisaachar bheet ke beech likhe chit laae |","meaning_en":"painting with care on the wall living beings, animals, gods and demons.","page":677,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਅਉਰ ਸਭੈ ਰਚਨਾ ਜਗ ਹੂ ਕੀ ਲਿਖੀ ਕਹਿ ਲਉ ਕਬਿ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਸੁਨਾਏ।","roman":"Aur sabhai rachnaa jag hoo kee likhee kahi lau kabi syaam sunaae |","meaning_en":"And all the rest of the world's creation she painted; how far, says the poet Shyam, can it be told?","page":677,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਉ ਇਹ ਆਇ ਸਮੁਛਤ ਕੈ ਬਹੀਆ ਗਹਿ ਯਾ ਸਭ ਹੀ ਦਰਸਾਏ। ੨੧੯੮।","roman":"Tau ih aai samuchhat kai baheeaa gahi yaa sabh hee darsaae | 2198 |","meaning_en":"Then she came and, explaining, took her by the arm and showed her all of it.","page":677,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[2199],"number_text":"੨੧੯੯।","page":677,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜਉ ਬਹੀਆ ਗਹਿ ਕੈ ਇਹ ਕੀ ਉਨ ਚਿਤ੍ਰ ਸਭੈ ਇਹ ਕਉ ਦਰਸਾਏ।","roman":"Jau baheeaa gahi kai ih kee un chitr sabhai ih kau darsaae |","meaning_en":"When, holding her arm, she showed her all the pictures,","page":677,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਦੇਖਤਿ ਦੇਖਤਿ ਗੀ ਤਿਹ ਠਾ ਜਹ ਦ੍ਵਾਰਵਤੀ ਬ੍ਰਿਜਨਾਥ ਬਨਾਏ।","roman":"Dekhti dekhti gee tih thaa jah dvaaravtee brijnaath banaae |","meaning_en":"looking and looking they came to the place where Dwarka, built by the Lord of Braj, was drawn.","page":677,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸੰਬਰ ਕੋ ਅਰਿ ਥੋ ਜਿਹ ਠਉਰ ਲਿਖਿਯੋ ਇਹ ਤਾ ਪਿਖਿ ਨੈਨ ਨਿਵਾਏ।","roman":"Sanbar ko ari tho jih thaur likhiyo ih taa pikhi nain nivaae |","meaning_en":"Where the enemy of Sambar was drawn, she looked at him and lowered her eyes.","page":677,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਸੰਬਰ ਕੋ ਅਰਿ: Pradyumna, slayer of the demon Sambar."},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਾ ਸੂਅ ਦੇਖਿ ਕਹਿਯੋ ਇਹ ਭਾਤਿ ਸਹੀ ਮੇਰੇ ਪ੍ਰੀਤਮ ਏ ਸਖੀ ਪਾਏ। ੨੧੯੯।","roman":"Taa sooa dekhi kahiyo ih bhaati sahee mere preetam e sakhee paae | 2199 |","meaning_en":"Seeing his son, she spoke thus: \"Truly, friend, this is the beloved I found.\"","page":677,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਤਾ ਸੂਅ: his son, i.e. Anirudh."}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਚੌਪਈ","gurmukhi":"ਚੌਪਈ","roman":"Chaupaee","meaning_en":"Chaupai.","page":677,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[2200],"number_text":"੨੨੦੦।","page":677,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕਹਿਯੋ ਸਖੀ ਅਬ ਢੀਲ ਨ ਕੀਜੈ। ਪ੍ਰੀਤਮ ਮੁਹਿ ਮਿਲਾਇ ਕੈ ਦੀਜੈ।","roman":"Kahiyo sakhee ab dheel na keejai | preetam muhi milaai kai deejai |","meaning_en":"She said, \"Friend, make no delay now; bring my beloved and unite me with him.","page":677,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਬ ਸਜਨੀ ਇਹ ਕਾਰਜ ਕੈ ਹੋ। ਜੀਵ ਦਾਨ ਤਬ ਮੋਕਹ ਦੈ ਹੋ। ੨੨੦੦।","roman":"Jab sajnee ih kaaraj kai ho | jeev daan tab mokah dai ho | 2200 |","meaning_en":"When, dear friend, you do this task, then you will grant me the gift of life.\"","page":677,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","gurmukhi":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","roman":"Savaiyaa","meaning_en":"Savaiya.","page":677,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[2201],"number_text":"੨੨੦੧।","page":677,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਯੌ ਬਤੀਯਾ ਸੁਨਿ ਕੈ ਭਈ ਚੀਲ ਚਲੀ ਉਡਿ ਦ੍ਵਾਰਵਤੀ ਮਹਿ ਆਈ।","roman":"Yau bateeyaa suni kai bhaee cheel chalee udi dvaaravtee mahi aaee |","meaning_en":"Hearing these words she became a kite, and flew off and came to Dwarka.","page":677,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਚੀਲ: kite (bird)."},{"gurmukhi":"ਪੌਤ੍ਰ ਹੁਤੋ ਜਿਹ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਜੂ ਕੋ ਛਪਿ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਭਨੈ ਤਿਹ ਬਾਤ ਸੁਨਾਈ।","roman":"Pautr huto jih syaam joo ko chhapi syaam bhanai tih baat sunaaee |","meaning_en":"To the grandson of Shyam, says Shyam, she secretly told the matter:","page":677,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਏਕ ਤ੍ਰੀਯਾ ਅਟਕੀ ਤੁਮ ਪੈ ਤੁਹਿ ਲ੍ਯਾਇਬੇ ਕੇ ਹਿਤ ਹਉ ਹੂ ਪਠਾਈ।","roman":"Ek treeyaa atkee tum pai tuhi lyaaibe ke hit hau hoo pathaaee |","meaning_en":"\"A woman's heart is set on you; I have been sent to bring you.","page":677,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਾ ਤੇ ਚਲੋ ਤਹ ਬੇਗ ਬਲਾਇ ਲਿਉ ਮੇਟਿ ਸਭੈ ਚਿਤ ਕੀ ਦੁਚਿਤਾਈ। ੨੨੦੧।","roman":"Taa te chalo tah beg balaai liu meti sabhai chit kee duchitaaee | 2201 |","meaning_en":"So come there quickly, I implore you, and wipe away all the doubt in your mind.\"","page":677,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਬਲਾਇ ਲਿਉ: 'I take your troubles on myself', an expression of fond entreaty; read so."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[2202],"number_text":"੨੨੦੨।","page":678,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਬੈਠ ਸੁਨਾਇ ਕੈ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਭਨੈ ਤਿਹ ਆਪਨੋ ਰੂਪ ਪ੍ਰਤਛ ਦਿਖਾਯੋ।","roman":"Baith sunaai kai syaam bhanai tih aapno roop pratachh dikhaayo |","meaning_en":"Sitting and speaking to him, says Shyam, she showed him her own form plainly.","page":678,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜੋ ਤ੍ਰੀਯ ਮੋ ਪਰ ਹੈ ਅਟਕੀ ਤਿਹ ਜਾਇ ਪਿਖੋ ਮਨੁ ਯਾਹਿ ਲੁਭਾਯੋ।","roman":"Jo treey mo par hai atkee tih jaai pikho manu yaahi lubhaayo |","meaning_en":"\"Go and see the woman whose heart is set on me\": his mind was enticed by this.","page":678,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਖੈਚ ਨਿਖੰਗ ਕਸਿਯੋ ਕਟਿ ਸੋ ਧਨੁ ਲੈ ਚਲਿਬੇ ਕਹੁ ਸਾਜ ਬਨਾਯੋ।","roman":"Khaich nikhang kasiyo kati so dhanu lai chalibe kahu saaj banaayo |","meaning_en":"He drew his quiver tight at his waist and, taking his bow, made ready to go.","page":678,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਦੂਤੀ ਕੋ ਸੰਗ ਲਏ ਅਪਨੇ ਇਹ ਤਾ ਤ੍ਰੀਅ ਲਿਆਵਨ ਕਾਜ ਸਿਧਾਯੋ। ੨੨੦੨।","roman":"Dootee ko sang lae apne ih taa treea liaavan kaaj sidhaayo | 2202 |","meaning_en":"Taking the go-between with him, he set off to fetch that woman.","page":678,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਦੂਤੀ: female messenger/go-between."}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","gurmukhi":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","roman":"Dohraa","meaning_en":"Dohra.","page":678,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[2203],"number_text":"੨੨੦੩।","page":678,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸੰਗ ਲਯੋ ਅਨਰੁਧ ਕੋ ਦੂਤੀ ਹਰਖ ਬਢਾਇ।","roman":"Sang layo anrudh ko dootee harakh badhaai |","meaning_en":"The go-between, her joy growing, took Anirudh along","page":678,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਊਖਾ ਕੋ ਪੁਰ ਥੋ ਜਹਾ ਤਹਾ ਪਹੂਚੀ ਆਇ। ੨੨੦੩।","roman":"Ookhaa ko pur tho jahaa tahaa pahoochee aai | 2203 |","meaning_en":"and arrived at the place where Usha's city was.","page":678,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਸੋਰਠਾ","gurmukhi":"ਸੋਰਠਾ","roman":"Sorthaa","meaning_en":"Sortha.","page":678,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[2204],"number_text":"੨੨੦੪।","page":678,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਤ੍ਰੀਅ ਪੀਅ ਦਯੋ ਮਿਲਾਇ ਚਤੁਰ ਤ੍ਰੀਅ ਕਰਿ ਚਤੁਰਤਾ।","roman":"Treea peea dayo milaai chatur treea kari chaturtaa |","meaning_en":"The clever woman, by her cleverness, brought the woman and the beloved together.","page":678,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕੀਯੋ ਭੋਗ ਸੁਖ ਪਾਇ ਊਖਾ ਅਰੁ ਅਨਰੁਧ ਮਿਲ। ੨੨੦੪।","roman":"Keeyo bhog sukh paai ookhaa aru anrudh mil | 2204 |","meaning_en":"Usha and Anirudh met and made love, finding pleasure.","page":678,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","gurmukhi":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","roman":"Savaiyaa","meaning_en":"Savaiya.","page":678,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[2205],"number_text":"੨੨੦੫।","page":678,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਚਾਰਿ ਪ੍ਰਕਾਰ ਕੋ ਭੋਗ ਕੀਓ ਨਰ ਨਾਰਿ ਹੁਲਾਸ ਹੀਯੈ ਮੈ ਬਢੈ ਕੈ।","roman":"Chaari prakaar ko bhog keeo nar naari hulaas heeyai mai badhai kai |","meaning_en":"Man and woman made love in four ways, with delight swelling in their hearts,","page":678,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਆਸਨ ਕੋਕ ਕੇ ਬੀਚ ਜਿਤੇ ਕਬਿ ਭਾਖਤ ਹੈ ਸੁ ਸਬੈ ਇਨ ਕੈ ਕੈ।","roman":"Aasan kok ke beech jite kabi bhaakhat hai su sabai in kai kai |","meaning_en":"performing all the postures that the poets describe in the Kok.","page":678,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਕੋਕ: the Koka-shastra, a treatise on love."},{"gurmukhi":"ਬਾਤ ਕਹੀ ਅਨਰੁਧ ਕਛੂ ਮੁਸਕਾਇ ਤ੍ਰੀਆ ਸੰਗ ਨੈਨ ਨਚੈ ਕੈ।","roman":"Baat kahee anrudh kachhoo muskaai treeaa sang nain nachai kai |","meaning_en":"Anirudh, smiling, said something to the woman, with dancing eyes:","page":678,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਿਉ ਹਮਰੀ ਤੁਮ ਹੁਇ ਰਹੀ ਸੁੰਦਰਿ ਤਿਉ ਹਮ ਹੂ ਤੁਮਰੇ ਰਹੈ ਹ੍ਵੈ ਕੈ। ੨੨੦੫।","roman":"Jiu hamree tum hui rahee sundri tiu ham hoo tumre rahai hvai kai | 2205 |","meaning_en":"\"As you have become mine, beautiful one, so I too will remain yours.\"","page":678,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[2206],"number_text":"੨੨੦੬।","page":678,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸੁੰਦਰ ਥੀ ਜੁ ਧੁਜਾ ਨ੍ਰਿਪ ਕੀ ਸੁ ਗਿਰੀ ਭੂਅ ਪੈ ਲਖਿ ਭੂਪਤਿ ਪਾਯੋ।","roman":"Sundar thee ju dhujaa nrip kee su giree bhooa pai lakhi bhoopti paayo |","meaning_en":"The king's beautiful banner fell to the ground; the king saw it.","page":678,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜੋ ਬਰੁ ਦਾਨ ਦਯੋ ਮੁਹਿ ਰੁਦ੍ਰ ਵਹੈ ਪ੍ਰਗਟਿਯੋ ਚਿਤ ਮੈ ਸੁ ਜਨਾਯੋ।","roman":"Jo baru daan dayo muhi rudr vahai pragtiyo chit mai su janaayo |","meaning_en":"\"The boon Rudra gave me has now come to pass,\" he realised in his mind.","page":678,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਉ ਹੀ ਲਉ ਆਇ ਕਹੀ ਇਕ ਯੌ ਤੁਮਰੀ ਦੁਹਿਤਾ ਗ੍ਰਿਹ ਮੋ ਕੋਊ ਆਯੋ।","roman":"Tau hee lau aai kahee ik yau tumree duhitaa grih mo ko'oo aayo |","meaning_en":"Just then someone came and said, \"Someone has come into your daughter's house.\"","page":678,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਯੌ ਨ੍ਰਿਪ ਬਾਤ ਚਲਿਯੋ ਸੁਨਿ ਕੈ ਅਪਨੇ ਚਿਤ ਮੈ ਅਤਿ ਰੋਸ ਬਢਾਯੋ। ੨੨੦੬।","roman":"Yau nrip baat chaliyo suni kai apne chit mai ati ros badhaayo | 2206 |","meaning_en":"Hearing this, the king set out, with great rage swelling in his heart.","page":678,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[2207],"number_text":"੨੨੦੭।","page":678,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਆਵਤ ਹੀ ਕਰਿ ਸਸਤ੍ਰ ਸੰਭਾਰਤ ਕੋਪ ਭਯੋ ਚਿਤਿ ਰੋਸ ਬਢਾਯੋ।","roman":"Aavat hee kari sasatr sanbhaarat kop bhayo chiti ros badhaayo |","meaning_en":"On arriving, grasping his weapons, he became furious, rage swelling in his heart.","page":678,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਾਨ੍ਹ ਕੇ ਪੌਤ੍ਰ ਸੋ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਭਨੈ ਦੁਹਿਤਾ ਹੂ ਕੇ ਮੰਦਰਿ ਜੁਧੁ ਮਚਾਯੋ।","roman":"Kaanh ke pautr so syaam bhanai duhitaa hoo ke mandri judhu machaayo |","meaning_en":"says Shyam, he fought with Krishna's grandson in his daughter's palace.","page":678,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਹੁਇ ਬਿਸੰਭਾਰ ਪਰਿਯੋ ਜਬ ਸੋ ਤਬ ਹੀ ਇਹ ਕੇ ਕਰਿ ਭੀਤਰ ਆਯੋ।","roman":"Hui bisanbhaar pariyo jab so tab hee ih ke kari bheetar aayo |","meaning_en":"When he (Anirudh) fell senseless, he came into his hands.","page":678,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Subject of the first half understood as Anirudh; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਨਾਦ ਬਜਾਇ ਦਿਖਾਇ ਸਭੋ ਬਲੁ ਲੈ ਇਹ ਕੋ ਨ੍ਰਿਪ ਧਾਮਿ ਸਿਧਾਯੋ। ੨੨੦੭।","roman":"Naad bajaai dikhaai sabho balu lai ih ko nrip dhaami sidhaayo | 2207 |","meaning_en":"Sounding his horn and showing all his strength, the king took him and went home.","page":678,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[2208],"number_text":"੨੨੦੮।","page":678,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕਾਨ੍ਹ ਕੇ ਪੌਤ੍ਰ ਕੋ ਬਾਧ ਕੈ ਭੂਪ ਫਿਰਿਯੋ ਉਤ ਨਾਰਦ ਜਾਇ ਸੁਨਾਈ।","roman":"Kaanh ke pautr ko baadh kai bhoop phiriyo ut naarad jaai sunaaee |","meaning_en":"Having bound Krishna's grandson, the king turned back; on the other side Narad went and told the news:","page":678,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਾਨ੍ਹ ਚਲੋ ਉਠਿ ਬੈਠੇ ਕਹਾ ਅਪੁਨੀ ਜਦੁਵੀ ਸਭ ਸੈਨ ਬਨਾਈ।","roman":"Kaanh chalo uthi baithe kahaa apunee jaduvee sabh sain banaaee |","meaning_en":"\"Krishna, rise and go! Why are you sitting? Make ready your whole Yadava army.\"","page":678,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਯੌ ਸੁਨਿ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਚਲੇ ਬਤੀਯਾ ਅਪੁਨੇ ਚਿਤ ਮੈ ਅਤਿ ਕਰੋਧ ਬਢਾਈ।","roman":"Yau suni syaam chale bateeyaa apune chit mai ati karodh badhaaee |","meaning_en":"Hearing this, Shyam set out, with great anger swelling in his heart,","page":678,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸਸਤ੍ਰ ਸੰਭਾਰਿ ਸਭੈ ਰਿਸ ਸੋ ਜਿਨ ਕੋ ਅਸ ਤੇਜੁ ਲਖਿਯੋ ਨਹਿ ਜਾਈ। ੨੨੦੮।","roman":"Sasatr sanbhaari sabhai ris so jin ko as teju lakhiyo nahi jaaee | 2208 |","meaning_en":"grasping all his weapons in fury, his radiance such that it could not be beheld.","page":678,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","gurmukhi":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","roman":"Dohraa","meaning_en":"Dohra.","page":679,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[2209],"number_text":"੨੨੦੯।","page":679,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਬਤੀਆ ਸੁਨਿ ਮੁਨਿ ਕੀ ਸਕਲ ਜਦੁਪਤਿ ਸੈਨ ਬਨਾਇ।","roman":"Bateeaa suni muni kee sakal jadupti sain banaai |","meaning_en":"Hearing the sage's words, the Lord of the Yadavs prepared his whole army","page":679,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਹਿ ਭੂਪਤਿ ਕੋ ਪੁਰ ਹੁਤੋ ਤਹਿ ਹੀ ਪਹੁਚਿਯੋ ਆਇ। ੨੨੦੯।","roman":"Jahi bhoopti ko pur huto tahi hee pahuchiyo aai | 2209 |","meaning_en":"and arrived at the place where the king's city was.","page":679,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","gurmukhi":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","roman":"Savaiyaa","meaning_en":"Savaiya.","page":679,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[2110],"number_text":"੨੧੧੦।","page":679,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਆਵਤ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਜੀ ਕੋ ਸੁਨਿ ਕੈ ਨ੍ਰਿਪ ਮੰਤ੍ਰ ਪੁਛਿਯੋ ਤਿਨ ਮੰਤ੍ਰਨ ਦੀਨੋ।","roman":"Aavat syaam jee ko suni kai nrip mantr puchhiyo tin mantran deeno |","meaning_en":"Hearing of Shyam's approach, the king asked for counsel, and the ministers gave it.","page":679,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਏਕ ਕਹੀ ਹਮ ਜੋ ਦੁਹਿਤਾ ਇਹ ਦੈ ਸੁ ਕਹਿਯੋ ਤੁਹਿ ਮਾਨਿ ਨ ਲੀਨੋ।","roman":"Ek kahee ham jo duhitaa ih dai su kahiyo tuhi maani na leeno |","meaning_en":"One said, \"We said you should give this daughter (in marriage), but you did not heed what was said.","page":679,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਮਾਗ ਲਯੋ ਸਿਵ ਤੇ ਰਨ ਕੋ ਬਰੁ ਜਾਨਤ ਹੈ ਤੂ ਭਯੋ ਮਤਿ ਹੀਨੋ।","roman":"Maag layo siv te ran ko baru jaanat hai too bhayo mati heeno |","meaning_en":"You asked Shiva for a boon of battle; know that you have lost your wits.","page":679,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਛੋਰਿ ਹੋ ਦ੍ਵੈ ਕਰਿ ਕੇ ਕਰ ਆਜੁ ਸੁ ਸ੍ਰੀ ਬ੍ਰਿਜਨਾਥ ਇਹੈ ਪ੍ਰਨ ਕੀਨੋ। ੨੧੧੦।","roman":"Chhori ho dvai kari ke kar aaju su sree brijnaath ihai pran keeno | 2110 |","meaning_en":"The Lord of Braj has vowed that today he will leave you with only two arms.\"","page":679,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Verse number printed ੨੧੧੦ (2110), out of sequence; read as 2210."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[2211],"number_text":"੨੨੧੧।","page":679,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਮਾਨੋ ਤੋ ਬਾਤ ਕਹੋ ਨ੍ਰਿਪ ਏਕ ਜੋ ਸ੍ਰਉਨਨ ਮੈ ਹਿਤ ਕੈ ਧਰੀਐ।","roman":"Maano to baat kaho nrip ek jo sraunan mai hit kai dhareeai |","meaning_en":"If you will heed, O king, I will say one thing, which you should keep in your ears kindly:","page":679,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਦੁਹਿਤਾ ਅਨਰੁਧ ਕੋ ਲੈ ਅਪੁਨੇ ਸਗਿ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਕੇ ਪਾਇਨ ਪੈ ਪਰੀਐ।","roman":"Duhitaa anrudh ko lai apune sagi syaam ke paain pai pareeai |","meaning_en":"take your daughter and Anirudh with you and fall at Shyam's feet.","page":679,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤੁਮਰੇ ਨ੍ਰਿਪ ਪਾਇ ਪਰੈ ਸੁਨੀਐ ਨਹੀ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਕੇ ਸੰਗਿ ਕਬੈ ਲਰੀਐ।","roman":"Tumre nrip paai parai suneeai nahee syaam ke sangi kabai lareeai |","meaning_en":"Fall at his feet, O king, listen, and never fight with Shyam.","page":679,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਅਰਿ ਹੋ ਨ ਜੋ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਭਨੈ ਹਰਿ ਸੋ ਭੂਅ ਪੈ ਤਬ ਰਾਜੁ ਸਦਾ ਕਰੀਐ। ੨੨੧੧।","roman":"Ari ho na jo syaam bhanai hari so bhooa pai tab raaju sadaa kareeai | 2211 |","meaning_en":"If you do not stand against Hari, says Shyam, then you may rule on earth forever.","page":679,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਅਰਿ ਹੋ ਨ ਜੋ: read as 'if you do not stand firm (against him)'; uncertain."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[2212],"number_text":"੨੨੧੨।","page":679,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸ੍ਰੀ ਬ੍ਰਿਜ ਨਾਇਕ ਜੋ ਰਿਸ ਕੈ ਰਨ ਮੈ ਕਰਿ ਜੋ ਧਨੁ ਸਾਰੰਗ ਲੈ ਹੈ।","roman":"Sree brij naaik jo ris kai ran mai kari jo dhanu saarang lai hai |","meaning_en":"When the Lord of Braj in anger takes up his bow Sarang in battle,","page":679,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਉਨ ਬਲੀ ਪ੍ਰਗਟਿਯੋ ਭੂਅ ਪੈ ਤੁਮ ਹੂ ਨ ਕਹੋ ਬਲਿ ਜੋ ਠਹਰੈ ਹੈ।","roman":"Kaun balee pragtiyo bhooa pai tum hoo na kaho bali jo thahrai hai |","meaning_en":"what mighty one has appeared on earth, tell us yourself, whose strength will hold before him?","page":679,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜੋ ਹਠ ਕੈ ਭਿਰਿ ਹੈ ਤਿਹ ਸੋ ਤਿਹ ਕਉ ਛਿਨ ਮੈ ਜਮਲੋਕਿ ਪਠੈ ਹੈ।","roman":"Jo hath kai bhiri hai tih so tih kau chhin mai jamloki pathai hai |","meaning_en":"Whoever obstinately fights with him, him he will send in an instant to the world of Yama.","page":679,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਅਉਰ ਭੁਜਾ ਕਟਿ ਕੈ ਤੁਮਰੀ ਸਬ ਦ੍ਵੈ ਭੁਜ ਰਾਖਿ ਤ੍ਵੈ ਪ੍ਰਾਨ ਬਚੈ ਹੈ। ੨੨੧੨।","roman":"Aur bhujaa kati kai tumree sab dvai bhuj raakhi tvai praan bachai hai | 2212 |","meaning_en":"And cutting off all your arms, leaving only two, he will spare your life.\"","page":679,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[2213],"number_text":"੨੨੧੩।","page":679,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਮੰਤ੍ਰੀ ਕੀ ਬਾਤ ਨ ਮਾਨਤ ਭਯੋ ਨ੍ਰਿਪ ਆਪਨੋ ਓਜ ਅਖੰਡ ਜਨਾਯੋ।","roman":"Mantree kee baat na maanat bhayo nrip aapno oj akhand janaayo |","meaning_en":"The king did not heed the minister's words and displayed his unbroken might.","page":679,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸਸਤ੍ਰ ਸੰਭਾਰ ਕੈ ਹਾਥਨ ਮੈ ਫੁਨਿ ਬੀਰਨ ਮੈ ਅਤਿ ਹੀ ਗਰਬਾਯੋ।","roman":"Sasatr sanbhaar kai haathan mai phuni beeran mai ati hee garbaayo |","meaning_en":"Grasping his weapons in his hands, he grew very proud among his warriors.","page":679,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸੈਨ ਪ੍ਰਚੰਡ ਹੁਤੋ ਜਿਤਨੋ ਤਿਸ ਕਉ ਨ੍ਰਿਪ ਆਪਨੇ ਧਾਮਿ ਬੁਲਾਯੋ।","roman":"Sain prachand huto jitno tis kau nrip aapne dhaami bulaayo |","meaning_en":"All the fierce army he had, the king summoned to his palace.","page":679,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਰੁਦ੍ਰ ਮਨਾਇ ਜਨਾਇ ਘਨੋ ਬਲੁ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਜੂ ਸੋ ਲਰਬੈ ਕਹੁ ਧਾਯੋ। ੨੨੧੩।","roman":"Rudr manaai janaai ghano balu syaam joo so larbai kahu dhaayo | 2213 |","meaning_en":"Propitiating Rudra and showing great strength, he rushed to fight with Shyam.","page":679,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[2214],"number_text":"੨੨੧੪।","page":679,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਉਤ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਜੂ ਬਾਨ ਚਲਾਵਤ ਭਯੋ ਇਤ ਤੇ ਦਸ ਸੈ ਭੁਜ ਬਾਨ ਚਲਾਏ।","roman":"Ut syaam joo baan chalaavat bhayo it te das sai bhuj baan chalaae |","meaning_en":"From there Shyam loosed arrows; from here the thousand-armed one loosed arrows.","page":679,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਾਦਵ ਆਵਤ ਭੇ ਉਤ ਤੇ ਇਤ ਤੇ ਇਨ ਕੇ ਸਭ ਹੀ ਭਟ ਧਾਏ।","roman":"Jaadav aavat bhe ut te it te in ke sabh hee bhat dhaae |","meaning_en":"The Yadavs came on from that side; from this side all his warriors charged.","page":679,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਘਾਇ ਕਰੈ ਮਿਲ ਆਪਸ ਮੈ ਤਿਨ ਯੌ ਉਪਮਾ ਕਬਿ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਸੁਨਾਏ।","roman":"Ghaai karai mil aapas mai tin yau upmaa kabi syaam sunaae |","meaning_en":"They struck wounds on one another; the poet Shyam gives this simile:","page":679,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਮਾਨਹੁ ਫਾਗੁਨ ਕੀ ਰੁਤਿ ਭੀਤਰ ਖੇਲਨ ਬੀਰ ਬਸੰਤਹਿ ਆਏ। ੨੨੧੪।","roman":"Maanhu phaagun kee ruti bheetar khelan beer basanthi aae | 2214 |","meaning_en":"as if in the season of Phagun the heroes had come to play at Basant.","page":679,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Phagun/Basant: spring festival of colour; blood likened to the colours thrown."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[2215],"number_text":"੨੨੧੫।","page":679,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਏਕ ਭਿਰੇ ਕਰਵਾਰਿਨ ਸੌ ਭਟ ਏਕ ਭਿਰੇ ਬਰਛੀ ਕਰਿ ਲੈ ਕੈ।","roman":"Ek bhire karvaarin sau bhat ek bhire barchhee kari lai kai |","meaning_en":"Some warriors clashed with swords, some fought taking spears in hand,","page":679,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਏਕ ਕਟਾਰਿਨ ਸੰਗ ਭਿਰੇ ਕਬਿ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਭਨੈ ਅਤਿ ਰੋਸਿ ਬਢੈ ਕੈ।","roman":"Ek kataarin sang bhire kabi syaam bhanai ati rosi badhai kai |","meaning_en":"some fought with daggers, says the poet Shyam, their rage swelling;","page":679,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਬਾਨ ਕਮਾਨਨ ਕਉ ਇਕ ਬੀਰ ਸੰਭਾਰਤ ਭੇ ਅਤਿ ਕ੍ਰੁਧਤ ਹ੍ਵੈ ਕੈ।","roman":"Baan kamaanan kau ik beer sanbhaarat bhe ati krudhat hvai kai |","meaning_en":"some heroes, in great fury, took up bows and arrows.","page":680,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਉਤੁਕ ਦੇਖਤ ਭਯੋ ਉਤ ਭੂਪ ਇਤੈ ਬ੍ਰਿਜ ਨਾਇਕ ਆਨੰਦ ਕੈ ਕੈ। ੨੨੧੫।","roman":"Kautuk dekhat bhayo ut bhoop itai brij naaik aanand kai kai | 2215 |","meaning_en":"Over there the king watched the spectacle; on this side the Lord of Braj was full of joy.","page":680,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[2216],"number_text":"੨੨੧੬।","page":680,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜਾ ਭਟ ਆਹਵ ਮੈ ਕਬਿ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਕਹੈ ਭਗਵਾਨ ਸੋ ਜੁਧੁ ਮਚਾਯੋ।","roman":"Jaa bhat aahav mai kabi syaam kahai bhagvaan so judhu machaayo |","meaning_en":"Whatever warrior in the battle, says the poet Shyam, fought with the Lord,","page":680,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਾਹੀ ਕੋ ਏਕ ਹੀ ਬਾਨ ਸੋ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਧਰਾ ਪਰਿ ਕੈ ਬਿਨੁ ਪ੍ਰਾਨ ਗਿਰਾਯੋ।","roman":"Taahee ko ek hee baan so syaam dharaa pari kai binu praan giraayo |","meaning_en":"him Shyam struck down lifeless to the ground with a single arrow.","page":680,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜੋ ਧਨੁ ਬਾਨਿ ਸੰਭਾਰਿ ਬਲੀ ਕੋਊ ਅਉ ਇਹ ਕੇ ਰਿਸਿ ਊਪਰ ਆਯੋ।","roman":"Jo dhanu baani sanbhaari balee ko'oo au ih ke risi oopar aayo |","meaning_en":"Whatever mighty one, grasping bow and arrows, came at him in anger,","page":680,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸੋ ਕਬਿ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਭਨੇ ਅਪਨੈ ਗ੍ਰਿਹਿ ਕੇ ਫਿਰਿ ਜੀਵਤ ਜਾਨ ਨ ਪਾਯੋ। ੨੨੧੬।","roman":"So kabi syaam bhane apnai grihi ke phiri jeevat jaan na paayo | 2216 |","meaning_en":"says the poet Shyam, did not get back to his own house alive.","page":680,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[2217],"number_text":"੨੨੧੭।","page":680,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਗੋਕੁਲ ਨਾਥ ਜੂ ਬੈਰਿਨ ਸੋ ਕਬਿ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਭਨੈ ਜਬ ਹੀ ਰਨ ਮਾਡਿਯੋ।","roman":"Gokul naath joo bairin so kabi syaam bhanai jab hee ran maadiyo |","meaning_en":"When the Lord of Gokul, says the poet Shyam, made war on the enemies,","page":680,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜੇਤਿਕ ਸਤ੍ਰਨ ਸਾਮੁਹੇ ਭੇ ਰਿਸਿ ਸੋ ਸਭਿ ਗਿਧ ਸ੍ਰਿੰਗਾਲਨ ਬਾਡਿਯੋ।","roman":"Jetik satran saamuhe bhe risi so sabhi gidh sringaalan baadiyo |","meaning_en":"all the foes who came before him he angrily shared out to the vultures and jackals.","page":680,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਪਤਿ ਰਥੀ ਗਜਿ ਬਾਜ ਘਨੇ ਬਿਨੁ ਪ੍ਰਾਨ ਕੀਏ ਕੋਊ ਜੀਤ ਨ ਛਾਡਿਯੋ।","roman":"Pati rathee gaji baaj ghane binu praan kee'e ko'oo jeet na chhaadiyo |","meaning_en":"Many foot-soldiers, chariot-warriors, elephants and horses he made lifeless; he left no one living.","page":680,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਕੋਊ ਜੀਤ ਨ ਛਾਡਿਯੋ: read ਜੀਤ as ਜੀਵਤ 'alive'; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਦੇਵ ਸਰਾਹਤ ਭੇ ਸਭ ਹੀ ਸੁ ਭਲੇ ਭਗਵਾਨ ਅਖੰਡਨ ਖਾਡਿਯੋ। ੨੨੧੭।","roman":"Dev saraahat bhe sabh hee su bhale bhagvaan akhandan khaadiyo | 2217 |","meaning_en":"All the gods praised him: \"Well done, the Lord has broken the unbreakable.\"","page":680,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[2218],"number_text":"੨੨੧੮।","page":680,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜੀਤੇ ਸਭੈ ਭਯ ਭੀਤ ਭਏ ਤਜਿ ਆਹਵ ਕੋ ਸਭ ਹੀ ਭਟ ਭਾਗੇ।","roman":"Jeete sabhai bhay bheet bhae taji aahav ko sabh hee bhat bhaage |","meaning_en":"All who were conquered became afraid; leaving the battlefield, all the warriors fled.","page":680,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਠਾਢੋ ਬਨਾਸੁਰ ਥੋ ਜਿਹ ਠਉਰ ਸਭੈ ਚਲਿ ਕੈ ਤਿਹ ਪਾਇਨ ਲਾਗੇ।","roman":"Thaadho banaasur tho jih thaur sabhai chali kai tih paain laage |","meaning_en":"Where Banasur stood, they all went and fell at his feet.","page":680,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਛੂਟ ਗਯੋ ਸਭਹੂਨ ਤੇ ਧੀਰਜ ਤ੍ਰਾਸਹਿ ਕੇ ਰਸ ਮੈ ਅਨੁਰਾਗੇ।","roman":"Chhoot gayo sabhhoon te dheeraj traashi ke ras mai anuraage |","meaning_en":"All had lost their courage and were steeped in the mood of terror.","page":680,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਭਾਖਤ ਭੇ ਨ੍ਰਿਪ ਸੋ ਭਜੀਐ ਬਚ ਹੈ ਨ ਕੋਊ ਬ੍ਰਿਜਨਾਥ ਕੇ ਆਗੇ। ੨੨੧੮।","roman":"Bhaakhat bhe nrip so bhajeeai bach hai na ko'oo brijnaath ke aage | 2218 |","meaning_en":"They said to the king, \"Let us flee; no one will survive before the Lord of Braj.\"","page":680,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[2219],"number_text":"੨੨੧੯।","page":680,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਭੀਰ ਪਰੀ ਜਬ ਭੂਪਤਿ ਪੈ ਤਬ ਆਪਨੇ ਜਾਨ ਕੈ ਈਸ ਨਿਹਾਰਿਯੋ।","roman":"Bheer paree jab bhoopti pai tab aapne jaan kai ees nihaariyo |","meaning_en":"When distress fell on the king, the Lord (Shiva), seeing him as his own, looked to him.","page":680,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸੰਤ ਸਹਾਇ ਕੋ ਜਾਇ ਭਿਰਿਯੋ ਬ੍ਰਿਜ ਨਾਇਕ ਸੋ ਚਿਤ ਬੀਚ ਬਿਚਾਰਿਯੋ।","roman":"Sant sahaai ko jaai bhiriyo brij naaik so chit beech bichaariyo |","meaning_en":"He, the helper of saints, considered in his mind going to fight the Lord of Braj.","page":680,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Read as Shiva deciding to help his devotee; ਸੰਤ ਸਹਾਇ 'helper of the devout'; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਆਯੁਧ ਲੈ ਅਪਨੇ ਸਭ ਹੀ ਹਰਿ ਓਰ ਸੁ ਜੁਧ ਕੇ ਕਾਜ ਸਿਧਾਰਿਯੋ।","roman":"Aayudh lai apne sabh hee hari or su judh ke kaaj sidhaariyo |","meaning_en":"Taking all his weapons, he set off toward Hari for the battle.","page":680,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਆਵਤ ਹੀ ਸੁ ਕਹੋ ਅਬ ਹਉ ਜਿਹ ਭਾਤਿ ਦੁਹੂ ਤਿਹ ਠਾ ਰਨ ਪਾਰਿਯੋ। ੨੨੧੯।","roman":"Aavat hee su kaho ab hau jih bhaati duhoo tih thaa ran paariyo | 2219 |","meaning_en":"Now I tell how, as soon as he arrived, the two waged war in that place.","page":680,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[2220],"number_text":"੨੨੨੦।","page":680,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਰੁਦ੍ਰ ਹ੍ਵੈ ਰੁਦ੍ਰ ਜਬੈ ਰਨ ਮੈ ਕਬਿ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਭਨੈ ਰਿਸਿ ਨਾਦ ਬਜਾਯੋ।","roman":"Rudr hvai rudr jabai ran mai kabi syaam bhanai risi naad bajaayo |","meaning_en":"When Rudra, becoming wrathful in the battle, says the poet Shyam, angrily sounded his horn,","page":680,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਰੁਦ੍ਰ ਹ੍ਵੈ ਰੁਦ੍ਰ: wordplay, Rudra becoming 'rudra' (terrible)."},{"gurmukhi":"ਸੂਰ ਨ ਕਾਹੂੰ ਤੇ ਨੈਕੁ ਟਿਕਿਯੋ ਗਯੋ ਭਾਜ ਗਏ ਨ ਰਤੀ ਕੁ ਦ੍ਰਿੜਾਯੋ।","roman":"Soor na kaahoon te naiku tikiyo gayo bhaaj gae na ratee ku driraayo |","meaning_en":"no warrior held his ground at all; they ran, and none stayed firm even a little.","page":680,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸਤ੍ਰਨ ਕੇ ਦੁਹੂ ਸਤ੍ਰਨ ਸੰਗ ਲੈ ਰੋਖ ਹਲੀ ਸੁ ਸੋਊ ਡਰ ਪਾਯੋ।","roman":"Satran ke duhoo satran sang lai rokh halee su so'oo dar paayo |","meaning_en":"Halli (Balram), who had taken on the enemies of both his foes in fury, he too felt fear.","page":680,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Obscure line; ਸਤ੍ਰਨ ਕੇ ਦੁਹੂ ਸਤ੍ਰਨ ਸੰਗ ਲੈ unclear; given as best reading; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਸ੍ਰੀ ਬ੍ਰਿਜਨਾਥ ਸੋ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਭਨੈ ਤਬ ਹੀ ਸਿਵ ਆਇ ਕੈ ਜੁਧੁ ਮਚਾਯੋ। ੨੨੨੦।","roman":"Sree brijnaath so syaam bhanai tab hee siv aai kai judhu machaayo | 2220 |","meaning_en":"Then, says Shyam, Shiva came and waged war with the Lord of Braj.","page":680,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[2221],"number_text":"੨੨੨੧।","page":680,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜੇ ਸਭ ਘਾਇ ਚਲਾਵਤ ਭਯੋ ਸਿਵ ਤੇ ਸਭ ਹੀ ਬ੍ਰਿਜਨਾਥ ਬਚਾਏ।","roman":"Je sabh ghaai chalaavat bhayo siv te sabh hee brijnaath bachaae |","meaning_en":"All the blows Shiva struck, the Lord of Braj warded off.","page":680,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਉਨ ਸਮੈ ਸਿਵ ਕੋ ਆਪੁਨੇ ਸਭ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਭਨੇ ਤਕਿ ਘਾਇ ਲਗਾਏ।","roman":"Taun samai siv ko aapune sabh syaam bhane taki ghaai lagaae |","meaning_en":"At that time, says Shyam, he took aim and struck all his own blows on Shiva.","page":680,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜੁਧੁ ਕੀਯੋ ਬਹੁ ਭਾਤਿ ਦੁਹੂ ਜਿਹ ਕੋ ਸਭ ਹੀ ਸੁਰ ਦੇਖਨ ਆਏ।","roman":"Judhu keeyo bahu bhaati duhoo jih ko sabh hee sur dekhan aae |","meaning_en":"The two fought in many ways, and all the gods came to watch.","page":680,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਅੰਤਿ ਖਿਸਾਇ ਰਿਸਾਇ ਕ੍ਰਿਪਾ ਨਿਧਿ ਏਕ ਗਦਾ ਹੂੰ ਸੋ ਰੁਦ੍ਰ ਗਿਰਾਏ। ੨੨੨੧।","roman":"Anti khisaai risaai kripaa nidhi ek gadaa hoon so rudr giraae | 2221 |","meaning_en":"At last, vexed and angered, the Treasure of Mercy felled Rudra with a single mace-blow.","page":680,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਚੌਪਈ","gurmukhi":"ਚੌਪਈ","roman":"Chaupaee","meaning_en":"Chaupai.","page":681,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[2222],"number_text":"੨੨੨੨।","page":681,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜਬ ਰੁਦ੍ਰਹਿ ਹਰਿ ਘਾਇ ਲਗਾਯੋ। ਬਿਸੁਧੋ ਕਰਿ ਕਰਿ ਭੂਮਿ ਗਿਰਾਯੋ।","roman":"Jab rudrahi hari ghaai lagaayo | bisudho kari kari bhoomi giraayo |","meaning_en":"When Hari struck Rudra a blow and felled him senseless to the ground,","page":681,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸੰਕਿਤ ਭਯੋ ਨ ਫਿਰਿ ਧਨੁ ਤਾਨਿਯੋ। ਸ੍ਰੀ ਜਦੁਬੀਰ ਸਹੀ ਪ੍ਰਭੁ ਜਾਨਿਯੋ। ੨੨੨੨।","roman":"Sankit bhayo na phiri dhanu taaniyo | sree jadubeer sahee prabhu jaaniyo | 2222 |","meaning_en":"he grew afraid and did not draw his bow again; he knew the hero of the Yadavs truly as the Lord.","page":681,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਸੋਰਠਾ","gurmukhi":"ਸੋਰਠਾ","roman":"Sorthaa","meaning_en":"Sortha.","page":681,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[2223],"number_text":"੨੨੨੩।","page":681,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਰੁਦ੍ਰ ਕੋਪ ਦਯੋ ਤ੍ਯਾਗ ਜਦੁਪਤਿ ਕੋ ਬਲੁ ਹੇਰ ਕੈ।","roman":"Rudr kop dayo tyaag jadupti ko balu her kai |","meaning_en":"Seeing the might of the Lord of the Yadavs, Rudra gave up his anger,","page":681,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਪਾਇਨ ਲਾਗਿਯੋ ਆਇ ਰਹਿਯੋ ਚਰਨ ਗਹਿ ਹਰ ਦੋਊ। ੨੨੨੩।","roman":"Paain laagiyo aai rahiyo charan gahi har do'oo | 2223 |","meaning_en":"came and fell at his feet; Har remained clasping both his feet.","page":681,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਹਰ: Shiva."}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","gurmukhi":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","roman":"Savaiyaa","meaning_en":"Savaiya.","page":681,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[2224],"number_text":"੨੨੨੪।","page":681,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਰੁਦ੍ਰ ਕੀ ਦੇਖਿ ਦਸਾ ਇਹ ਭਾਤਿ ਸੁ ਆਪਹਿ ਜੁਧੁ ਕੋ ਭੂਪਤਿ ਆਯੋ।","roman":"Rudr kee dekhi dasaa ih bhaati su aaphi judhu ko bhoopti aayo |","meaning_en":"Seeing Rudra's state thus, the king himself came to the battle.","page":681,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਭਨੈ ਦਸ ਸੈ ਭੁਜ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਕੇ ਊਪਰ ਬਾਨਨ ਓਘ ਚਲਾਯੋ।","roman":"Syaam bhanai das sai bhuj syaam ke oopar baanan ogh chalaayo |","meaning_en":"says Shyam, the thousand-armed one loosed a flood of arrows upon Shyam.","page":681,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਓਘ ਜੋ ਆਵਤ ਬਾਨਨ ਕੋ ਸਭ ਹੀ ਹਰਿ ਮਾਰਗ ਮੈ ਨਿਵਰਾਯੋ।","roman":"Ogh jo aavat baanan ko sabh hee hari maarag mai nivraayo |","meaning_en":"The flood of arrows that came, Hari turned aside on the way.","page":681,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸਾਰੰਗ ਆਪੁਨ ਹਾਥ ਬਿਖੈ ਧਰਿ ਕੈ ਅਰਿ ਕੋ ਬਹੁ ਘਾਇਨ ਘਾਯੋ। ੨੨੨੪।","roman":"Saarang aapun haath bikhai dhari kai ari ko bahu ghaain ghaayo | 2224 |","meaning_en":"Taking his own Sarang in his hand, he struck the enemy with many wounds.","page":681,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[2225],"number_text":"੨੨੨੫।","page":681,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸ੍ਰੀ ਬ੍ਰਿਜ ਨਾਇਕ ਕ੍ਰੁਧਿਤ ਹੁਇ ਅਪਨੇ ਕਰ ਮੈ ਧਨ ਸਾਰੰਗ ਲੈ ਕੈ।","roman":"Sree brij naaik krudhit hui apne kar mai dhan saarang lai kai |","meaning_en":"The Lord of Braj, enraged, taking the bow Sarang in his hand,","page":681,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜੁਧੁ ਮਚਾਵਤ ਭਯੋ ਦਸ ਸੈ ਭੁਜ ਸੋ ਅਤਿ ਓਜ ਅਖੰਡ ਜਨੈ ਕੈ।","roman":"Judhu machaavat bhayo das sai bhuj so ati oj akhand janai kai |","meaning_en":"waged war with the thousand-armed one, showing unbroken strength.","page":681,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਅਉਰ ਹਨੇ ਬਲਵੰਡ ਘਨੇ ਕਬਿ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਭਨੈ ਅਤਿ ਪਉਰਖ ਕੈ ਕੈ।","roman":"Aur hane balvand ghane kabi syaam bhanai ati paurakh kai kai |","meaning_en":"And he slew many more mighty ones, says the poet Shyam, with great valour.","page":681,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਛੋਰਿ ਦਯੋ ਤਿਹ ਭੂਪਤਿ ਕੋ ਰਨ ਮੈ ਤਿਹ ਕੀ ਸੁ ਭੁਜਾ ਫੁਨ ਦ੍ਵੈ ਕੈ। ੨੨੨੫।","roman":"Chhori dayo tih bhoopti ko ran mai tih kee su bhujaa phun dvai kai | 2225 |","meaning_en":"He let that king go in the battle, leaving him with two arms.","page":681,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"speaker","name":"ਕਬਿਯੋ ਬਾਚ","gurmukhi":"ਕਬਿਯੋ ਬਾਚ","roman":"Kabiyo baach","meaning_en":"The poet said:","page":681,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","gurmukhi":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","roman":"Savaiyaa","meaning_en":"Savaiya.","page":681,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[2226],"number_text":"੨੨੨੬।","page":681,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਬਾਹ ਸਹੰਸ੍ਰ ਕਹੋ ਤੁਮ ਹੀ ਅਬ ਲਉ ਜਗ ਮੈ ਨਰ ਕਾਹੂ ਕੀ ਹੋਈ।","roman":"Baah sahansr kaho tum hee ab lau jag mai nar kaahoo kee hoee |","meaning_en":"Tell me yourselves: up to now, has any man in the world had a thousand arms?","page":681,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਅਉਰ ਕਹੋ ਕਿਹ ਭੂਪ ਇਤੀ ਅਪਨੇ ਗ੍ਰਿਹ ਬੀਚ ਸੰਪਤਿ ਸਮੋਈ।","roman":"Aur kaho kih bhoop itee apne grih beech sanpti samoee |","meaning_en":"And tell me, what king has held so much wealth in his house?","page":681,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਏਤੇ ਪੈ ਸੰਤ ਸੁਨੋ ਹਿਤ ਕੈ ਸਿਵ ਸੋ ਛਰੀਯਾ ਪੁਨਿ ਰਾਖਤ ਹੋਈ।","roman":"Ete pai sant suno hit kai siv so chhareeyaa puni raakhat hoee |","meaning_en":"On top of this, listen lovingly, O saints, he even kept Shiva as his doorkeeper.","page":681,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਛਰੀਯਾ: read as 'staff-bearer, guard'; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਾ ਨ੍ਰਿਪ ਕੋ ਬਰੁ ਯਾ ਬਿਧਿ ਈਸ ਦਯੋ ਜਗਦੀਸ ਕੀਓ ਭਯੋ ਸੋਈ। ੨੨੨੬।","roman":"Taa nrip ko baru yaa bidhi ees dayo jagdees keeo bhayo soee | 2226 |","meaning_en":"To that king the Lord (Shiva) gave the boon in this way, but what the Lord of the World did, that came to pass.","page":681,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਚੌਪਈ","gurmukhi":"ਚੌਪਈ","roman":"Chaupaee","meaning_en":"Chaupai.","page":681,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[2227],"number_text":"੨੨੨੭।","page":681,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜਬ ਤਿਹ ਮਾਤਿ ਬਾਤ ਸੁਨਿ ਪਾਈ। ਨ੍ਰਿਪ ਹਾਰਿਯੋ ਜੀਤਿਯੋ ਜਦੁਰਾਈ।","roman":"Jab tih maati baat suni paaee | nrip haariyo jeetiyo jaduraaee |","meaning_en":"When his mother heard the news that the king was defeated and the King of the Yadavs had won,","page":681,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸਭ ਤਜਿ ਬਸਤ੍ਰ ਨਗਨ ਹੁਇ ਆਈ। ਆਇ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਕੋ ਦਈ ਦਿਖਾਈ। ੨੨੨੭।","roman":"Sabh taji basatr nagan hui aaee | aai syaam ko daee dikhaaee | 2227 |","meaning_en":"she cast off all her clothes and came naked; she came and showed herself to Shyam.","page":681,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[2228],"number_text":"੨੨੨੮।","page":681,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਤਬ ਪ੍ਰਭੁ ਦ੍ਰਿਗ ਨੀਚੇ ਹੁਇ ਰਹਿਯੋ। ਨੈਕ ਨ ਜੂਝਬ ਚਿਤ ਮੋ ਚਹਿਯੋ।","roman":"Tab prabhu drig neeche hui rahiyo | naik na joojhab chit mo chahiyo |","meaning_en":"Then the Lord kept his eyes lowered, and did not wish to fight in his heart at all.","page":681,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਭੂਪਤਿ ਸਮੈ ਭਜਨ ਕੋ ਪਾਯੋ। ਭਾਜਿ ਗਯੋ ਨਹਿ ਜੁਧ ਮਚਾਯੋ। ੨੨੨੮।","roman":"Bhoopti samai bhajan ko paayo | bhaaji gayo nahi judh machaayo | 2228 |","meaning_en":"The king got the chance to flee; he ran away and did not fight.","page":681,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਭਜਨ: here 'fleeing'; read so."}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"speaker","name":"ਨ੍ਰਿਪ ਬਾਚ ਬੀਰਨ ਸੋ","gurmukhi":"ਨ੍ਰਿਪ ਬਾਚ ਬੀਰਨ ਸੋ","roman":"Nrip baach beeran so","meaning_en":"The king said to his warriors:","page":682,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","gurmukhi":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","roman":"Savaiyaa","meaning_en":"Savaiya.","page":682,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[2229],"number_text":"੨੨੨੯।","page":682,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਬਿਪਤ ਹੁਇ ਬਹੁ ਘਾਇਨ ਸੋ ਨ੍ਰਿਪ ਬੀਰਨ ਮੈ ਇਹ ਭਾਤਿ ਉਚਾਰਿਯੋ।","roman":"Bipat hui bahu ghaain so nrip beeran mai ih bhaati uchaariyo |","meaning_en":"Distressed by many wounds, the king spoke thus among his warriors:","page":682,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕੋਊ ਨ ਸੂਰ ਟਿਕਿਯੋ ਮੁਹ ਅਗ੍ਰਜ ਹਉ ਜਿਹ ਕੀ ਰਿਸਿ ਓਰਿ ਪਧਾਰਿਯੋ।","roman":"Ko'oo na soor tikiyo muh agraj hau jih kee risi ori padhaariyo |","meaning_en":"\"No warrior held firm before me, against whomever I went in anger.","page":682,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਗਾਜਬੋ ਮੋ ਸੁਨਿ ਕੈ ਅਬ ਲਉ ਕਿਨਹੂ ਕਰ ਮੈ ਨਹੀ ਸਸਤ੍ਰ ਸੰਭਾਰਿਯੋ।","roman":"Gaajbo mo suni kai ab lau kinhoo kar mai nahee sasatr sanbhaariyo |","meaning_en":"Hearing my roar, till now no one has taken a weapon in hand.","page":682,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਏਤੇ ਪੈ ਮੋ ਸੰਗਿ ਆਇ ਭਿਰਿਯੋ ਸੁ ਸਹੀ ਬ੍ਰਿਜ ਨਾਇਕ ਬੀਰੇ ਨਿਹਾਰਿਯੋ। ੨੨੨੯।","roman":"Ete pai mo sangi aai bhiriyo su sahee brij naaik beere nihaariyo | 2229 |","meaning_en":"Yet this one came and fought with me; truly I have seen the Lord of Braj to be a hero.\"","page":682,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[2230],"number_text":"੨੨੩੦।","page":682,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸ੍ਰੀ ਜਦੁਬੀਰ ਤੇ ਜੋ ਸਹਸ੍ਰ ਭੁਜ ਭਾਜਿ ਗਯੋ ਨਹਿ ਜੁਧੁ ਮਚਾਯੋ।","roman":"Sree jadubeer te jo sahasr bhuj bhaaji gayo nahi judhu machaayo |","meaning_en":"The thousand-armed one who fled from the hero of the Yadavs and did not fight,","page":682,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਦ੍ਵੈ ਭੁਜ ਦੇਖਿ ਭਈ ਅਪੁਨੀ ਅਪੁਨੇ ਚਿਤ ਮੈ ਅਤਿ ਤ੍ਰਾਸ ਬਢਾਯੋ।","roman":"Dvai bhuj dekhi bhaee apunee apune chit mai ati traas badhaayo |","meaning_en":"seeing that he had only two arms left, grew greatly afraid in his heart.","page":682,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸੋ ਜਗ ਮੈ ਜਸੁ ਲੇਤਿ ਭਯੋ ਜਿਨਿ ਸ੍ਰੀ ਬ੍ਰਿਜ ਨਾਥਹਿ ਕੋ ਗੁਨ ਗਾਯੋ।","roman":"So jag mai jasu leti bhayo jini sree brij naathhi ko gun gaayo |","meaning_en":"He who sang the praises of the Lord of Braj gained fame in the world.","page":682,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਉ ਹੀ ਜਥਾ ਮਤਿ ਸੰਤ ਪ੍ਰਸਾਦ ਤੇ ਯੌ ਕਹਿ ਕੈ ਕਛੁ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਸੁਨਾਯੋ। ੨੨੩੦।","roman":"Tau hee jathaa mati sant prasaad te yau kahi kai kachhu syaam sunaayo | 2230 |","meaning_en":"So, according to his understanding and by the grace of the saints, Shyam has related this.","page":682,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[2231],"number_text":"੨੨੩੧।","page":682,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਆਵਤ ਭਯੋ ਰਿਸ ਕੈ ਸਿਵ ਜੂ ਫਿਰਿ ਆਪੁਨੇ ਸੰਗ ਸਭੈ ਗਨ ਲੈ ਕੈ।","roman":"Aavat bhayo ris kai siv joo phiri aapune sang sabhai gan lai kai |","meaning_en":"Then Shiva came again in anger, bringing all his ganas with him.","page":682,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਗਨ: Shiva's attendants."},{"gurmukhi":"ਸ੍ਰੀ ਜਦੁਬੀਰ ਕੇ ਸਾਮੁਹੇ ਬੀਰ ਕਹੈ ਕਬਿ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਸੁ ਕ੍ਰੁਧਿਤ ਹ੍ਵੈ ਕੈ।","roman":"Sree jadubeer ke saamuhe beer kahai kabi syaam su krudhit hvai kai |","meaning_en":"Before the hero of the Yadavs, says the poet Shyam, the warriors, enraged,","page":682,"flags":[{"code":"0x71","reason":"subjoined letter typed after the vowel/nasal sign; put in Unicode order (same printed shape)"}],"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਬਾਨ ਕ੍ਰਿਪਾਨ ਗਦਾ ਬਰਛੀ ਗਹਿ ਆਵਤ ਭੇ ਰਿਸਿ ਨਾਦ ਬਜੈ ਕੈ।","roman":"Baan kripaan gadaa barchhee gahi aavat bhe risi naad bajai kai |","meaning_en":"came on grasping arrows, swords, maces and spears, sounding their horns in anger.","page":682,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸੋ ਛਿਨ ਮੈ ਪ੍ਰਭ ਜੂ ਸਭ ਬੀਰ ਦਏ ਫੁਨਿ ਅੰਤ ਕੇ ਧਾਮਿ ਪਠੈ ਕੈ। ੨੨੩੧।","roman":"So chhin mai prabh joo sabh beer dae phuni ant ke dhaami pathai kai | 2231 |","meaning_en":"In an instant the Lord sent all those warriors to the abode of death.","page":682,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[2232],"number_text":"੨੨੩੨।","page":682,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਏਕ ਹਨੇ ਜਦੁਰਾਇ ਗਦਾ ਗਹਿ ਏਕ ਬਲੀ ਰਿਪੁ ਸੰਬਰ ਘਾਏ।","roman":"Ek hane jaduraai gadaa gahi ek balee ripu sanbar ghaae |","meaning_en":"Some the King of the Yadavs slew, grasping his mace; some the mighty enemy of Sambar slew.","page":682,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਏਕ ਭਿਰੇ ਮੁਸਲੀਧਰ ਸੋ ਸੁ ਤੇ ਜੀਵਤ ਧਾਮ ਹੂ ਜਾਨ ਨ ਪਾਏ।","roman":"Ek bhire musleedhar so su te jeevat dhaam hoo jaan na paae |","meaning_en":"Some fought with the bearer of the pestle (Balram); they could not go home alive.","page":682,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਮੁਸਲੀਧਰ: Balram, who bears a pestle-club."},{"gurmukhi":"ਜੋ ਫਿਰਿ ਆਇ ਭਿਰੇ ਹਰਿ ਸੋ ਚਿਤ ਮੈ ਫੁਨਿ ਕੋਪ ਕੀ ਓਪ ਬਢਾਏ।","roman":"Jo phiri aai bhire hari so chit mai phuni kop kee op badhaae |","meaning_en":"Those who came again and fought with Hari, letting the flash of anger grow in their minds,","page":682,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਯੌ ਫਿਰਿ ਛੇਦਤ ਭਯੋ ਤਿਨ ਕਉ ਜੋਊ ਜੰਬੁਕ ਗੀਧਨ ਹਾਥਿ ਨ ਆਏ। ੨੨੩੨।","roman":"Yau phiri chhedat bhayo tin kau jo'oo janbuk geedhan haathi na aae | 2232 |","meaning_en":"he cut them down in such a way that they did not even reach the hands of the jackals and vultures.","page":682,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[2233],"number_text":"੨੨੩੩।","page":682,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਐਸੇ ਨਿਹਾਰਿ ਭਯੋ ਤਹਿ ਆਹਵ ਚਿਤ ਬਿਖੈ ਅਤਿ ਕ੍ਰੋਧ ਬਢਾਯੋ।","roman":"Aise nihaari bhayo tahi aahav chit bikhai ati krodh badhaayo |","meaning_en":"Seeing the battle go thus, he (Shiva) grew very angry in his heart.","page":682,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਠੋਕਿ ਭੁਜਾ ਅਪਨੀ ਦੋਊ ਆਪ ਹੀ ਹਾਥ ਲੈ ਆਪਨੈ ਨਾਦ ਬਜਾਯੋ।","roman":"Thoki bhujaa apnee do'oo aap hee haath lai aapnai naad bajaayo |","meaning_en":"Slapping both his arms, he took up and sounded his own horn himself.","page":682,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਿਉ ਕੁਪ ਅੰਧਕ ਦੈਤ ਪੈ ਧਾਵਤ ਭਯੋ ਤਿਮ ਕੋਪ ਕੈ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਪੈ ਧਾਯੋ।","roman":"Jiu kup andhak dait pai dhaavat bhayo tim kop kai syaam pai dhaayo |","meaning_en":"As he once rushed in anger at the demon Andhak, so in anger he rushed at Shyam.","page":682,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਯੌ ਉਪਜੀ ਉਪਮਾ ਲਰਬੇ ਕਹੁ ਕੇਹਰਿ ਸੋ ਜਨੁ ਕੇਹਰਿ ਆਯੋ। ੨੨੩੩।","roman":"Yau upjee upmaa larbe kahu kehri so janu kehri aayo | 2233 |","meaning_en":"This simile arose for the fight: as if a lion had come at a lion.","page":682,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[2234],"number_text":"੨੨੩੪।","page":682,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜੁਧ ਮੰਡਿਯੋ ਅਤਿ ਹੀ ਤਬਹੀ ਸਿਵ ਤਾਪ ਹੁਤੋ ਇਕ ਸੋਊ ਸੰਭਾਰਿਯੋ।","roman":"Judh mandiyo ati hee tabhee siv taap huto ik so'oo sanbhaariyo |","meaning_en":"When the battle was fierce, Shiva called up a fever that he had.","page":682,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਤਾਪ: fever; Shiva's fever (Maheshvara-jvara); read so."},{"gurmukhi":"ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਜੁ ਭੇਦ ਸਭੈ ਲਹਿ ਕੈ ਜੁਰ ਸੀਤ ਸੁ ਤਾਹੀ ਕੀ ਓਰਿ ਪਚਾਰਿਯੋ।","roman":"Syaam ju bhed sabhai lahi kai jur seet su taahee kee ori pachaariyo |","meaning_en":"Shyam, knowing the whole secret, sent the cold fever against it.","page":682,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਦੇਖਤ ਹੀ ਜੁਰ ਸੀਤ ਕਉ ਸੋ ਜੁਰ ਭਾਜਿ ਗਯੋ ਨ ਰਤੀ ਕੁ ਸੰਭਾਰਿਯੋ।","roman":"Dekhat hee jur seet kau so jur bhaaji gayo na ratee ku sanbhaariyo |","meaning_en":"As soon as it saw the cold fever, that fever fled and did not hold even a little.","page":682,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਯੌ ਉਪਮਾ ਉਪਜੀ ਜੀਅ ਮੈ ਬਦਰਾ ਬਹਿਯੋ ਜਾਤ ਬਿਯਾਰ ਕੋ ਮਾਰਿਯੋ। ੨੨੩੪।","roman":"Yau upmaa upjee jeea mai badraa bahiyo jaat biyaar ko maariyo | 2234 |","meaning_en":"This simile arose in the mind: as a cloud is driven off, struck by the wind.","page":682,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[2235],"number_text":"੨੨੩੫।","page":682,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਗਰਬ ਜਿਤੋ ਸਿਵ ਬੀਚ ਹੁਤੋ ਸਭ ਹੀ ਹਰਿ ਕ੍ਰੁਧ ਕੈ ਜੁਧੁ ਮਿਟਾਯੋ।","roman":"Garab jito siv beech huto sabh hee hari krudh kai judhu mitaayo |","meaning_en":"All the pride that was in Shiva, Hari in anger wiped out in the battle.","page":682,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜੋ ਤਿਨ ਤੀਰਨ ਬ੍ਰਿਸਟ ਕਰੀ ਤਿਹ ਤੇ ਸਰ ਏਕ ਨੇ ਭੇਟਨ ਪਾਯੋ।","roman":"Jo tin teeran brisat karee tih te sar ek ne bhetan paayo |","meaning_en":"Of the shower of arrows that he loosed, not a single arrow reached him.","page":682,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਅਉਰ ਜਿਤੇ ਗਨ ਸੰਗ ਹੁਤੇ ਸਭ ਕੋ ਹਰਿ ਘਾਇ ਘਨੇ ਸੰਗਿ ਘਾਯੋ।","roman":"Aur jite gan sang hute sabh ko hari ghaai ghane sangi ghaayo |","meaning_en":"All the ganas who were with him, Hari struck with many wounds.","page":683,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਐਸੋ ਨਿਹਾਰ ਕੈ ਪਉਰਖ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਗਨਪਤਿ ਪਾਇਨ ਸੋ ਲਪਟਾਯੋ। ੨੨੩੫।","roman":"Aiso nihaar kai paurakh syaam ganapti paain so laptaayo | 2235 |","meaning_en":"Seeing such valour of Shyam, Ganpati clung to his feet.","page":683,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਗਨਪਤਿ: lord of the ganas, here likely Shiva himself (or Ganesh); uncertain."}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"speaker","name":"ਸਿਵ ਬਾਚ","gurmukhi":"ਸਿਵ ਬਾਚ","roman":"Siv baach","meaning_en":"Shiva said:","page":683,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","gurmukhi":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","roman":"Savaiyaa","meaning_en":"Savaiya.","page":683,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[2236],"number_text":"੨੨੩੬।","page":683,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਭੂਲ ਪਰਿਯੋ ਪ੍ਰਭ ਮੈ ਘਟ ਕਾਮ ਕੀਯੋ ਤੁਮ ਸੋ ਜੁ ਪੈ ਜੁਧ ਚਹਿਯੋ।","roman":"Bhool pariyo prabh mai ghat kaam keeyo tum so ju pai judh chahiyo |","meaning_en":"\"O Lord, I made a mistake; I did a lowly thing in wishing for war with you.","page":683,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤੋ ਕਹਾ ਭਯੋ ਜੋ ਰਿਸਿ ਆਇ ਭਿਰਿਯੋ ਤੁ ਕਹਾ ਇਹ ਠਾ ਮੇਰੇ ਮਾਨ ਰਹਿਯੋ।","roman":"To kahaa bhayo jo risi aai bhiriyo tu kahaa ih thaa mere maan rahiyo |","meaning_en":"What came of it, that I came in anger and fought? What honour of mine remained here?","page":683,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤੁਮਰੇ ਗੁਨ ਗਾਵਤ ਹੀ ਸਹਸ ਫਨਿ ਅਉਰ ਚਤੁਰਾਨਨ ਹਾਰਿ ਰਹਿਯੋ।","roman":"Tumre gun gaavat hee sahas phani aur chaturaanan haari rahiyo |","meaning_en":"Singing your praises the thousand-hooded one and the four-faced one have grown weary.","page":683,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਸਹਸ ਫਨਿ: Sheshnag; ਚਤੁਰਾਨਨ: Brahma."},{"gurmukhi":"ਤੁਮਰੇ ਗੁਣ ਕਉਨ ਗਨੈ ਕਹ ਲਉ ਜਿਹ ਬੇਦ ਸਕੈ ਨਹਿ ਭੇਦ ਕਹਿਯੋ। ੨੨੩੬।","roman":"Tumre gun kaun ganai kah lau jih bed sakai nahi bhed kahiyo | 2236 |","meaning_en":"Who can count your virtues, and how far, when even the Vedas cannot tell your secret?\"","page":683,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"speaker","name":"ਕਬਿਯੋ ਬਾਚ","gurmukhi":"ਕਬਿਯੋ ਬਾਚ","roman":"Kabiyo baach","meaning_en":"The poet said:","page":683,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","gurmukhi":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","roman":"Savaiyaa","meaning_en":"Savaiya.","page":683,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[2237],"number_text":"੨੨੩੭।","page":683,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕਾ ਭਯੋ ਜੋ ਧਰਿ ਮੂੰਡ ਜਟਾ ਸੋ ਤਪੋਧਨ ਕੋ ਜਗ ਭੇਖ ਦਿਖਾਯੋ।","roman":"Kaa bhayo jo dhari moond jataa so tapodhan ko jag bhekh dikhaayo |","meaning_en":"What of it if one wears matted hair on the head and shows the world the garb of an ascetic?","page":683,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਾ ਭਯੋ ਜੁ ਕੋਊ ਲੋਚਨ ਮੂੰਦਿ ਭਲੀ ਬਿਧਿ ਸੋ ਹਰਿ ਕੋ ਗੁਨ ਗਾਯੋ।","roman":"Kaa bhayo ju ko'oo lochan moondi bhalee bidhi so hari ko gun gaayo |","meaning_en":"What of it if someone closes his eyes and sings Hari's praises in fine manner?","page":683,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਅਉਰ ਕਹਾ ਜੋ ਪੈ ਆਰਤੀ ਲੈ ਕਰਿ ਧੂਪ ਜਗਾਇ ਕੈ ਸੰਖ ਬਜਾਯੋ।","roman":"Aur kahaa jo pai aartee lai kari dhoop jagaai kai sankh bajaayo |","meaning_en":"And what of it if one takes the arti, lights incense and blows the conch?","page":683,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਕਹੈ ਤੁਮ ਹੀ ਨ ਕਹੋ ਬਿਨ ਪ੍ਰੇਮ ਕਿਹੂ ਬ੍ਰਿਜ ਨਾਇਕ ਪਾਯੋ। ੨੨੩੭।","roman":"Syaam kahai tum hee na kaho bin prem kihoo brij naaik paayo | 2237 |","meaning_en":"says Shyam, tell me yourselves: has anyone found the Lord of Braj without love?","page":683,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[2238],"number_text":"੨੨੩੮।","page":683,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਤਿਉ ਚਤੁਰਾਨਨ ਤਿਉਹੂ ਖੜਾਨਨ ਤਿਉ ਸਹਸਾਨਨ ਹੀ ਗੁਨ ਗਾਯੋ।","roman":"Tiu chaturaanan tiuhoo kharaanan tiu sahsaanan hee gun gaayo |","meaning_en":"So the four-faced one, so the six-faced one, so the thousand-faced one sang his praises;","page":683,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਖੜਾਨਨ: Kartikeya; ਸਹਸਾਨਨ: Sheshnag."},{"gurmukhi":"ਨਾਰਦ ਸਕ੍ਰ ਸਦਾ ਸਿਵ ਬ੍ਯਾਸ ਇਤੇ ਗੁਨ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਕੋ ਗਾਇ ਸੁਨਾਯੋ।","roman":"Naarad sakr sadaa siv byaas ite gun syaam ko gaai sunaayo |","meaning_en":"Narad, Indra, Sadashiv and Vyas, all these sang and recited Shyam's virtues.","page":683,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਚਾਰੋ ਈ ਬੇਦ ਨ ਭੇਦ ਲਹਿਯੋ ਜਗ ਖੋਜਤ ਹੈ ਸਭ ਪਾਰ ਨ ਪਾਯੋ।","roman":"Chaaro ee bed na bhed lahiyo jag khojat hai sabh paar na paayo |","meaning_en":"Even the four Vedas did not find his secret; the whole world searches and does not find his end.","page":683,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਭਨੈ ਤੁਮ ਹੀ ਨ ਕਹੋ ਬਿਨ ਪ੍ਰੇਮ ਕਹੂ ਬ੍ਰਿਜਨਾਥ ਰਿਝਾਯੋ। ੨੨੩੮।","roman":"Syaam bhanai tum hee na kaho bin prem kahoo brijnaath rijhaayo | 2238 |","meaning_en":"says Shyam, tell me yourselves: has anyone pleased the Lord of Braj without love?","page":683,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"speaker","name":"ਸਿਵ ਜੂ ਬਾਚ ਕਾਨ੍ਹ ਜੂ ਸੋ","gurmukhi":"ਸਿਵ ਜੂ ਬਾਚ ਕਾਨ੍ਹ ਜੂ ਸੋ","roman":"Siv joo baach kaanh joo so","meaning_en":"Shiva said to Krishna:","page":683,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","gurmukhi":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","roman":"Savaiyaa","meaning_en":"Savaiya.","page":683,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[2239],"number_text":"੨੨੩੯।","page":683,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਪਾਇ ਪਰਿਯੋ ਸਿਵ ਜੂ ਹਰਿ ਕੇ ਕਹਿਯੋ ਮੋ ਬਿਨਤੀ ਹਰਿ ਜੂ ਸੁਨਿ ਲੀਜੈ।","roman":"Paai pariyo siv joo hari ke kahiyo mo bintee hari joo suni leejai |","meaning_en":"Shiva fell at Hari's feet and said, \"O Hari, hear my plea.","page":683,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸੇਵਕ ਮਾਗਤ ਹੈ ਬਰੁ ਏਕ ਵਹੈ ਅਬ ਰੀਝਿ ਦਇਆ ਨਿਧਿ ਦੀਜੈ।","roman":"Sevak maagat hai baru ek vahai ab reejhi daiaa nidhi deejai |","meaning_en":"Your servant asks one boon; be pleased, Treasure of Compassion, and grant it now.","page":683,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਹੇਰਿ ਹਮੈ ਕਬਿ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਭਨੈ ਕਬਹੂੰ ਕਰੁਨਾ ਰਸ ਕੇ ਸੰਗਿ ਭੀਜੈ।","roman":"Heri hamai kabi syaam bhanai kabhoon karunaa ras ke sangi bheejai |","meaning_en":"Look on us, says the poet Shyam, and be moistened at times with the essence of compassion.","page":683,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਬਾਹੈ ਕਟੀ ਸਹਸ੍ਰਾਭੁਜ ਕੀ ਤੁ ਭਲੋ ਤਿਹ ਕੋ ਅਬ ਨਾਸੁ ਨ ਕੀਜੈ। ੨੨੩੯।","roman":"Baahai katee sahsraabhuj kee tu bhalo tih ko ab naasu na keejai | 2239 |","meaning_en":"The thousand-armed one's arms have been cut, and that is well; now do not destroy him.\"","page":683,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"speaker","name":"ਕਾਨ੍ਹ ਜੂ ਬਾਚ ਸਿਵ ਜੂ ਪ੍ਰਤਿ","gurmukhi":"ਕਾਨ੍ਹ ਜੂ ਬਾਚ ਸਿਵ ਜੂ ਪ੍ਰਤਿ","roman":"Kaanh joo baach siv joo prati","meaning_en":"Krishna said to Shiva:","page":683,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","gurmukhi":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","roman":"Savaiyaa","meaning_en":"Savaiya.","page":683,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[2240],"number_text":"੨੨੪੦।","page":683,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸੋ ਕਰਿਹੋ ਅਬ ਹਉ ਸੁਨਿ ਰੁਦ੍ਰ ਜੂ ਤੋ ਸੰਗਿ ਬੈਨ ਉਚਾਰਤ ਹਉ।","roman":"So kariho ab hau suni rudr joo to sangi bain uchaarat hau |","meaning_en":"\"Listen, Rudra, I will do that; I speak these words to you.","page":683,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਬਾਹੈ ਕਟੀ ਤਿਹ ਭੂਲਿ ਨਿਹਾਰਿ ਅਬ ਹਉ ਹੂ ਸੁ ਕ੍ਰੋਧ ਨਿਵਾਰਤ ਹਉ।","roman":"Baahai katee tih bhooli nihaari ab hau hoo su krodh nivaarat hau |","meaning_en":"His arms were cut for the error I saw in him; now I too set aside my anger.","page":683,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਪ੍ਰਹਲਾਦ ਕੋ ਪੌਤ੍ਰ ਕਹਾਵਤ ਹੈ ਸੁ ਇਹੈ ਜੀਅ ਮਾਹਿ ਬਿਚਾਰਤ ਹਉ।","roman":"Prahlaad ko pautr kahaavat hai su ihai jeea maahi bichaarat hau |","meaning_en":"He is called the grandson of Prahlad; this I consider in my heart.","page":684,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Banasur is son of Bali, grandson of Virochan, great-grandson of Prahlad; text says ਪੌਤ੍ਰ 'grandson'."},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਾ ਤੇ ਡੰਡ ਹੀ ਦੈ ਕਰਿ ਛੋਰਿ ਦਯੋ ਇਹ ਤੇ ਨਾਹਿ ਤਾਹਿ ਸੰਘਾਰਤ ਹਉ। ੨੨੪੦।","roman":"Taa te dand hee dai kari chhori dayo ih te naahi taahi sanghaarat hau | 2240 |","meaning_en":"Therefore I have let him go with only a punishment; for this reason I do not slay him.\"","page":684,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[2241],"number_text":"੨੨੪੧।","page":684,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਯੌ ਬਖਸਾਇ ਕੈ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਜੂ ਸੋ ਤਿਹ ਭੂਪ ਕੋ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਕੇ ਪਾਇਨ ਡਾਰੋ।","roman":"Yau bakhsaai kai syaam joo so tih bhoop ko syaam ke paain daaro |","meaning_en":"Having thus won Shyam's pardon, he (Shiva) laid that king at Shyam's feet:","page":684,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਭੂਲ ਕੈ ਭੂਪਤਿ ਕਾਮ ਕਰਿਯੋ ਅਬ ਹੇ ਪ੍ਰਭ ਜੂ ਤੁਮ ਕ੍ਰੋਧ ਨਿਵਾਰੋ।","roman":"Bhool kai bhoopti kaam kariyo ab he prabh joo tum krodh nivaaro |","meaning_en":"\"The king acted in error; now, O Lord, set aside your anger.","page":684,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਪੌਤ੍ਰ ਕੋ ਬ੍ਯਾਹ ਕਰੋ ਇਹ ਕੀ ਦੁਹਿਤਾ ਸੰਗਿ ਅਉਰ ਕਛੂ ਮਨ ਮੈ ਨ ਬਿਚਾਰੋ।","roman":"Pautr ko byaah karo ih kee duhitaa sangi aur kachhoo man mai na bichaaro |","meaning_en":"Marry your grandson to his daughter and think nothing else in your mind.\"","page":684,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਯੌ ਕਰਿ ਬ੍ਯਾਹ ਸੰਗ ਊਖਹ ਲੈ ਅਨਰੁਧ ਕੋ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਜੂ ਧਾਮਿ ਸਿਧਾਰੋ। ੨੨੪੧।","roman":"Yau kari byaah sang ookhah lai anrudh ko syaam joo dhaami sidhaaro | 2241 |","meaning_en":"Thus, after the marriage, taking Usha and Anirudh, Shyam went home.","page":684,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[2242],"number_text":"੨੨੪੨।","page":684,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜੋ ਸੁਨਿ ਹੈ ਗੁਨ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਜੂ ਕੇ ਫੁਨਿ ਅਉਰਨ ਤੇ ਅਰੁ ਆਪਨ ਗੈ ਹੈ।","roman":"Jo suni hai gun syaam joo ke phuni auran te aru aapan gai hai |","meaning_en":"Whoever hears the praises of Shyam from others, and sings them himself,","page":684,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਆਪਨ ਜੋ ਪੜ ਹੈ ਪੜਵਾਇ ਹੈ ਅਉਰ ਕਬਿਤਨ ਬੀਚ ਬਨੈ ਹੈ।","roman":"Aapan jo par hai parvaai hai aur kabitan beech banai hai |","meaning_en":"who reads them himself and has them read, and makes them into poems,","page":684,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸੋਵਤ ਜਾਗਤ ਧਾਵਤ ਧਾਮ ਸੁ ਸ੍ਰੀ ਬ੍ਰਿਜ ਨਾਇਕ ਕੀ ਸੁਧਿ ਲੈ ਹੈ।","roman":"Sovat jaagat dhaavat dhaam su sree brij naaik kee sudhi lai hai |","meaning_en":"who while sleeping, waking, running or at home keeps the Lord of Braj in remembrance,","page":684,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸੋਊ ਸਦਾ ਕਬਿ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਭਨੈ ਫੁਨਿ ਯਾ ਭਵ ਭੀਤਰ ਫੇਰਿ ਨ ਐ ਹੈ। ੨੨੪੨।","roman":"So'oo sadaa kabi syaam bhanai phuni yaa bhav bheetar pheri na ai hai | 2242 |","meaning_en":"says the poet Shyam, he will never come again into this world of births.","page":684,"meaning_status":"draft"}]}],"ending":{"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਇਤਿ ਸ੍ਰੀ ਦਸਮ ਸਿਕੰਧ ਪੁਰਾਣੇ ਬਚਿਤ੍ਰ ਨਾਟਕ ਗ੍ਰੰਥੇ ਕ੍ਰਿਸਨਾਵਤਾਰੇ ਥਾਣਾਸੁਰ","roman":"Iti sree dasam sikandh puraane bachitr naatak granthe krisnaavtaare thaanaasur","meaning_en":"Here ends, in the Dasam Sikandh Puran, in the Bachittar Natak Granth, in Krishnavatar, (the chapter of) Thanasur","page":684,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਥਾਣਾਸੁਰ: printed so; read as Banasur."},{"gurmukhi":"ਕੋ ਜੀਤਿ ਅਨਰੁਧ ਊਖਾ ਕੋ ਬ੍ਯਾਹ ਲਿਆਵਤ ਭਏ।","roman":"Ko jeeti anrudh ookhaa ko byaah liaavat bhae |","meaning_en":"being conquered and Usha being married to Anirudh and brought home.","page":684,"meaning_status":"draft"}],"page":684}});
